const IDX=[{"title": "Renown", "url": "rules-renown.html", "text": "Renown\n A turn-based strategy game of empire building, diplomacy, and domain mastery.\n"}, {"title": "Introduction", "url": "rules-introduction.html", "text": "Introduction\nWithin the Realm, Empires expand, specialize, confer, and when diplomacy fails\u2014battle. You will lead your humble Province to greatness. Charter new Settlements, build your economy, and negotiate your way to victory. Will your religion dominate the Realm? Will your economy grow until your wealth is undeniable? Can you build a world wonder? Can you extort your way to victory? Pick your Heritage, command your Domain, and pursue your Craft in this political grand strategy, where every action you attempt can be endorsed or condemned by your allies and other players.\nGame Synopsis\nRenown is a turn-based political strategy game for 1\u20137 players (3+ preferred) set in a medieval world of competing lords. Each player controls a growing empire \u2014 Settlements, Armies, and Holdings \u2014 but the game&#x27;s central tension isn&#x27;t military. It&#x27;s political.\nEvery action you want to take has to survive a vote. When you move your Army, build a road, or sabotage a rival, every other player at the table gets to spend political Influence to support or bury it. The strength of your relationships, the Alliances you&#x27;ve built, and the favors you&#x27;re owed decide whether your plans "}, {"title": "Reading These Rules", "url": "rules-reading-these-rules.html", "text": "Reading These Rules\nA few conventions make every rule in this book read the same way:\n\nmay marks something optional. If a rule doesn&#x27;t say may, it&#x27;s mandatory.\ncan&#x27;t and doesn&#x27;t are hard stops (see Core Principle 2).\nEffects are written by when they apply: While X is always on; When X / At X happens once, at that moment; an action&#x27;s Cost / Effect / Endorsed happens when you take the action.\nLimits are written by window: At the Start of the Empire Phase happens once, in that step; Each &lt;Phase&gt; happens every time that phase does; Once per &lt;Phase&gt; can be used once, only during that phase; Once per turn can be used once, in any phase \u2014 a trigger such as when an Army ends a Move action fires in whichever phase the Move happens.\nChoose one: marks a set of options from which you pick exactly one.\nItalic text is reminder, example, or strategy \u2014 it explains the rule but never changes it; the plain-text rule governs.\nCapitalized terms (Army, Envoy, Standing, Holding, Treaty\u2026) are defined terms \u2014 each section closes with a glossary of the terms it introduces, and the Index at the back lists every term with its page numbers.\n\nGlossary \u00b7 Reading the RulesTer"}, {"title": "Core Principles", "url": "rules-core-principles.html", "text": "Core Principles\n\nGranted Power. Any mechanic not explicitly described doesn&#x27;t function.\n\n\nSpecific over general. A more specific rule overrides a general one.\n\n    2.1 Example: Inquisitorial Palace \u2265 Established Cunning &gt; general Cunning rule.\n    2.2 When two effects conflict, the one that says can&#x27;t (or doesn&#x27;t) takes precedence over one that says you may or must.\n\nPublic information. All information is public: resources, Domains, Treaties, Armies, Holdings, and Garrisons are known to all players.\n\n\nOnce per turn, same target. A once-per-turn effect can&#x27;t be used on the same target twice in a turn.\n\n\nOne effect per Holding. A Holding has a single effect, active while the Holding is active.\n\n\nDamaged means inactive. A Damaged Holding or Infrastructure has no effect.\n\n\nTimer 0 resolves immediately. Any Timer whose initial value is 0 or less resolves at once.\n\n\nDo as much as possible. Follow as much of an effect as you can; ignore any part you can&#x27;t carry out.\n\n\nDice.\n\n    9.1 If a roll is modified beyond 10+, it automatically fails.\n    9.2 You can&#x27;t re-roll a re-roll, and you can&#x27;t re-roll a successful roll.\n    9.3 Effects that occur on a 1 o"}, {"title": "Resources", "url": "rules-resources.html", "text": "Resources\n\nGold / Treasury \u2014 your spendable wealth. Pays for Actions, upkeep, and Muster recruitment. Running out triggers Insolvency (see Treasury &amp; Upkeep).\nDomain Points \u2014 gain 1 each Rest Phase and spend it to raise a Domain value by 1 (see Domains &amp; Standings).\nInfluence \u2014 the weight you bring to Envoy votes: spend it to Support or Oppose other players&#x27; Envoys (see Actions &amp; Voting).\nRenown \u2014 the score of the table. Gained each Rest Phase and by completing Edicts; it sets the Era.\nPublic Order \u2014 the stability of your realm, raised by Faith and lowered by Doubt. Its band sets ongoing effects (see Public Order).\nFaith \u2014 devotion, generated mostly by Piety Holdings; each Faith raises your Public Order by 1.\nDoubt \u2014 instability; each Doubt lowers your Public Order by 1. Some powerful Holdings cost you Doubt; Cunning and Piety actions give it to others.\n"}, {"title": "The Turn", "url": "rules-the-turn.html", "text": "The Turn\nEach turn runs through five phases in order, then passes the Host and repeats:\n\nEmpire Phase \u2014 Start of the Empire Phase effects, the Season, Timers, Bandit Mechanics, Influence &amp; Envoys, income and upkeep, Public Order.\nCouncil Phase \u2014 a Council vote on a Domain; each player then performs one action of that Domain.\nEnvoy Phase \u2014 send all Envoys, a Forum, vote on every Envoy, then resolve them all (Diplomacy \u2192 Prowess \u2192 Cunning \u2192 Piety \u2192 Industry).\nBattle Phase \u2014 Skirmishes, Sieges, and Battles resolve.\nRest Phase \u2014 cleanup, advance the Season, score Renown, spend one Domain Point, pass the Host.\n\nThe Host. Each turn except Spring, one player is the Host. The starting player is always the player directly clockwise from the Host token, including in Spring. The role passes clockwise each Rest Phase (except in Spring). The Host runs most of the Empire Phase&#x27;s administration: collecting and distributing Trade Income, resolving Bandit Mechanics, and breaking ties (Council vote, Bandit targeting, and anything not otherwise resolvable). The Host Card carries the step-by-step detail.\nTimers\nMany actions set a Timer to a number of turns. Each Empire Phase, every active Tim"}, {"title": "Seasons", "url": "rules-seasons.html", "text": "Seasons\nThe Realm cycles through four Seasons. The current Season&#x27;s effect is applied during the Empire Phase, and the Rest Phase advances the Season by one. Each time the Season changes to Spring, the Year advances by 1.\nSeasonNameEffectWinterFreezingAll Armies gain Speed -5; Siege Timers don&#x27;t count down. Tax income collected.SpringPlantingNo Host, Bandit Actions, Trade Income, Council Phase, or Diplomacy Actions. Players don&#x27;t gain or spend Influence tokens. Bandit Camps Spawn.SummerCampaigningAll Armies gain Speed +3FallHarvestIncome from Holdings in Hamlets is doubled."}, {"title": "Table Setup", "url": "rules-table-setup.html", "text": "Table Setup\n\nDomain Board: set Renown to 1, set each player&#x27;s Standing in each Domain to 1, set Season to Summer, and set Public Order to 0.\nTactic Decks, Equipment &amp; Retinue Cards, Holding Tiles, Bandit Camps, and the various tokens.\n"}, {"title": "Setup Order", "url": "rules-setup-order.html", "text": "Setup Order\n\nSelect Map \u2014 choose the Hex Map.\nSelect Age \u2014 choose an Age and a starting Year within its range (see Ages). Every player starts Rising in that Age&#x27;s Domain: set that Domain to 3. In the Age of Renown, each player chooses their own Rising Domain. Turn 1 takes place in the starting Year.\nSelect Heritage \u2014 pick a Heritage Card (optional for new players).\nDetermine Host \u2014 give the Host Card to the most experienced player. If tied, to whoever wants to Host; if still tied, roll off.\nDeploy \u2014 taking turns from the starting player, each player places their capital Town within Range 4 of the board edge or corner. Then each player places their Hamlet exactly Range 2 from their Town. Then each player places their Outlaw Country: its first Territory exactly Range 2 from their Town, and no Outlaw Country Territory within Range 2 of their Hamlet.\nWild Outlaw Country \u2014 the Host scatters the remaining Outlaw Country zones over the unclaimed board (see Outlaw Country).\n\nAges\nAn Age sets the starting Year and which Domain every player starts Rising in.\nAgeStarting RisingStarting YearAge of FractureProwess0\u20131352Age of PlentyIndustry1352\u20131942Age of the TetramorphPiety1942\u20133066Age of"}, {"title": "Player Setup", "url": "rules-player-setup.html", "text": "Player Setup\n\nEmpire Tableau.\nCollect 10000 Gold, 2 Influence Tokens, and 1 Envoy.\nYou don&#x27;t begin the game with any Armies.\nFor the first turn, begin at the Council Phase instead of the Empire Phase.\n"}, {"title": "Action Mechanics", "url": "rules-action-mechanics.html", "text": "Action Mechanics\nSending an Envoy\nEnvoys are the currency of actions: to perform an action you send an Envoy during the Envoy Phase. Sending costs 1 Envoy, and you must be able to pay the action&#x27;s cost before you send it. Declare the Domain but not the action \u2014 &quot;I&#x27;d like to send a [Domain] Envoy.&quot; Envoys never target: you choose the action, and its target, only after the Envoy passes, so no one knows exactly what will happen until then.\nResolving an Envoy\nYour Envoy begins with Authority equal to your innate Authority in its Domain \u2014 Untested 1, Rising 2, Established 3, Sovereign 4 \u2014 plus any automatic Authority \u00b1X modifiers. (These come from your Holdings, Infrastructure, and Heritage, and apply on their own; you never spend Influence for them.) Diplomacy has no Standing; a Diplomacy Envoy begins with Authority set by the Era (Founding 1, Ascension 2, Eminence 3, Zenith 4).\nThen, clockwise from the starting player and skipping the sender, every other player may respond, with no talking during the vote:\n\nSupport X \u2014 spend X of your Influence to raise the Envoy&#x27;s net Authority.\nOppose X \u2014 spend X of your Influence to lower it.\nAbstain \u2014 spend nothing.\n\nYou s"}, {"title": "Influence", "url": "rules-influence.html", "text": "Influence\nEach Empire Phase, gain Influence from the following sources:\nSourceInfluence ChangeNotesEra+1/+2/+3/+4Based on the Current EraTrading Partners+1Per Trading Partner.Alliances+1Per Alliance Member.Infrastructure tier completed+1Per Infrastructure tier fully completed.Fully Mustered Army+1Per active Army of 25 Retinues.Condemned Envoy last turn-1Per Condemned Envoy last turn.At War-3While at War.Monuments &amp; Wonders+1Per active Monument or Wonder.Other sources+XFrom other effects like Holdings.\n"}, {"title": "Diplomacy Actions", "url": "rules-diplomacy-actions.html", "text": "Diplomacy Actions\nActionCostRequiresEffect (if passes)EndorsedSign TreatyNone\u2014Ask players to agree, then choose one and both sign it: Peace Treaty \u2014 end the war, set Truce Timer 5; Trade Agreement \u2014 begin trading next turn; Non-Aggression Pact \u2014 no Declare War (ending it via End Treaty gives both Truce Timer 5); Alliance \u2014 join, form, or invite to a Defensive or Military Alliance. \u2014 When acting on behalf of an Alliance, End Treaty requires all allies to agree.; A player can&#x27;t be in more than one Alliance.Faith +1.NegotiateNone\u2014Propose terms to a target; they agree or refuse. Terms may include gold, Settlement ownership, Territory, signing or ending a Treaty, or promises (non-binding). \u2014 If a promise goes unfulfilled, the affected player may Declare War on the promiser.; Also used to resolve Demand Tribute and Siege surrenders.Faith +1.End TreatyNone\u2014Choose a target with whom you have an active Treaty and no active Truce Timer; remove that Treaty. The target doesn&#x27;t need to agree.Faith +1.\nRule: Diplomatic Mission\nIf your Diplomacy Envoy passes or is endorsed but its action fails, you may send another Envoy in another Domain, resolved in the order it would be resolved alon"}, {"title": "Prowess Actions", "url": "rules-prowess-actions.html", "text": "Prowess Actions\nActionCostRequiresEffect (if passes)EndorsedMoveNone\u2014Move an Army up to its Speed in Territories. Then choose one: March \u2014 move up to 2\u00d7 Speed, lose 1 Endurance, take no other action; Battle \u2014 end adjacent to an at-war Army not in a Settlement, then begin a Battle; Lay Siege \u2014 end adjacent to an at-war Settlement, then begin a Siege. \u2014 Unless the move action was Endorsed, an Army may be the target of only one Move action per turn.; Presence limits where the Army may move (see Rule: Presence).; While an Army&#x27;s Battle or Siege Timer is active, it can&#x27;t be the target of actions.; When an Army performs the Battle action, it gains Seize the Initiative in that Battle&#x27;s first Skirmish.Perform another Move action (same or a different Army).Declare WarNoneRising ProwessChoose a non-allied player you have no NAP or active truce with. You and that player are now At War, and any Trade Agreements between you end. If the target is in a Defensive Alliance, every member is now At War with you. \u2014 If you are in a Military Alliance, then at the start of your next turn every member Declares War on the target and sends 1 fewer Envoy that turn.Perform a Move action.Pillage"}, {"title": "Cunning Actions", "url": "rules-cunning-actions.html", "text": "Cunning Actions\nActionCostRequiresEffect (if passes)EndorsedIntercept Caravan2000 gold\u2014Choose a player. The next turn that player is Host, Extort their Trade Income. If they have no Trade Income that turn, instead Extort 100 per their Craft. \u2014 This affects only a single turn&#x27;s trade income; normal income resumes afterward.Extort 2000.Foster Rebellion2000 gold\u2014Choose a player. At the next Bandit Mechanics step, place a Bandit Camp of 10 Retinues in their Outlaw Country. \u2014 If that player&#x27;s Outlaw Country has no room, expand it by one Territory and spawn there instead.Extort 2000.Raze2000 gold\u2014Choose another player&#x27;s Settlement, then choose one active Holding, active Infrastructure, or active Build Timer in it: that target becomes Damaged, and its effects are inactive until Repaired. A Damaged Build Timer doesn&#x27;t count down until Repaired. If an active Build Timer hasn&#x27;t been completed, instead, increase the Timer by 2. \u2014 A Wonder has Immune Razed and can&#x27;t be targeted.Extort 2000.Destabilize2000 gold\u2014Choose a player. In the next Winter phase, during the Extort step, Extort one settlement&#x27;s tax income. Each settlement can only be Destabilized once pe"}, {"title": "Piety Actions", "url": "rules-piety-actions.html", "text": "Piety Actions\nActionCostRequiresEffect (if passes)EndorsedSpread TruthDoubt 1\u2014Each non-allied player gains Doubt 1. Each allied player gains Faith 1.Recoup Doubt.Send MissionariesDoubt 1\u2014Choose a target player or Alliance. If the target is outside your Alliance, each player in it gains Doubt 2. If the target is inside your Alliance, each other allied player gains Faith 2.Recoup Doubt.TitheDoubt 1\u2014Choose a player. Extort 10% of their Treasury (round down to the nearest 100, minimum 0).Recoup Doubt.ConvertDoubt 1Sovereign PietyChoose another player&#x27;s closest non-capital Settlement; its Public Order must be -5 or lower. Lay Siege using only Settlement-type Siege modifiers (Settlement Size and Citadel) and set a Convert Timer. When it reaches 0, the Settlement joins your empire (see Capture). \u2014 If the target&#x27;s Public Order rises to 1 or higher before the timer reaches 0, the Convert fails and the timer is removed.Recoup Doubt.Sacred WarDoubt 1Sovereign PietyDeclare War on a non-ally you have no NAP or truce with, then immediately perform a Move action with one of your Armies. \u2014 While a Sacred War is active, neither player may Declare War on, Sign or End a Treaty with, Negotia"}, {"title": "Industry Actions", "url": "rules-industry-actions.html", "text": "Industry Actions\nActionCostRequiresEffect (if passes)EndorsedImprove2000 gold\u2014Choose one: Infrastructure \u2014 choose an unlocked, available Infrastructure and set a Build Timer equal to its build time; when it completes, the Infrastructure becomes active in every Settlement in your Province. Or Expand a Settlement one tier (Village to Town, Town to City, City to Metropolis), adding a Ward. \u2014 You must have at least one Infrastructure from the prior tier before building the next tier.; A Wonder is built in your capital.; To upgrade to City or Metropolis you must meet that tier&#x27;s requirements; otherwise set Build Timer 1.Recoup 2000.Repair0 gold\u2014Choose a Damaged Holding or Infrastructure in a Settlement you control and set Repair Timer 2. When it reaches 0, choose one: Restore \u2014 reactivate it with all effects; Demolish \u2014 remove the Holding tile from your Empire Tableau.Recoup 0.Build2000 gold\u2014Choose an inactive Settlement Ward you control, then choose a Holding with one complete line of its Mastery Chain under your control (and meet its other requirements) and set a Build Timer equal to its build time (usually 1). When it completes, place the Holding in an available Ward slot; its e"}, {"title": "Domains & Standings", "url": "rules-domains-standings.html", "text": "Domains &amp; Standings\nDomain Standings\nDomains are the identity of your character in Renown. As you gain Renown each turn, you gain a Domain Point, which you may spend in any of the four Domains. Each Domain Point raises your Domain value by 1 in that Domain. When your Domain value reaches 3, you become Rising in that Domain \u2014 you may spend one extra Influence on another player&#x27;s Envoy of that Domain, and your Envoys gain Authority +1. This continues at a Domain value of 6 (Established) and again at 10 (Sovereign).\nEach Standing you gain in a Domain makes you harder to oppose there and lets you oppose others more easily with your Influence. You also gain a unique effect at each Standing that makes it easier to achieve that Domain&#x27;s objectives. A Standing effect that lets you perform an action (Perform \u2026) is one-time: you use it at the Start of the next Empire Phase after you reach that Standing (a Standing you start the game with: Turn 1). Every other Standing effect applies for as long as you hold that Standing; its Each Empire Phase effects resolve at the Start of the Empire Phase.\nStanding &amp; Influence\nYour Standing in a Domain sets how much Influence you bring to"}, {"title": "Diplomacy & Treaties", "url": "rules-diplomacy-treaties.html", "text": "Diplomacy &amp; Treaties\nTreaties &amp; Alliances\nTreatySigned ViaEraEffectPeace TreatySign TreatyAnyEnds war between the two players; sets Truce Timer 5.Trade AgreementSign TreatyAnyBegin trading (Trade Income flows from next turn). Requires bordering, and each player has active Dirt Roads or a Can Trade effect.Non-Aggression PactSign TreatyAnyNeither player may Declare War on the other. Ending it via End Treaty gives both a Truce Timer 5.Military AllianceSign TreatyEminenceMutual offensive pact: if a member Declares War, all members Declare War on the target next turn (and send 1 fewer envoy).Defensive AllianceSign TreatyZenithMutual defense: attacking one member puts all members at war with the attacker.\nAlliance Rules:\nNew alliance members are added by unanimous agreement.A player cannot be in more than one alliance at a time.An alliance may remove a member via End Treaty if all others agree.\nVassalization\nTo vassalize a player:\n\nControl that player&#x27;s capital Settlement while the player has no other Settlements or Armies under their Control.\n\n\nAt the end of the Rest Phase, return every Settlement you Control that was chartered by that player to that player. You become thei"}, {"title": "Settlements", "url": "rules-settlements.html", "text": "Settlements\nSettlements are the primary vehicle of your Empire. They come in tiers: Village, Town, City, and a capital Metropolis. Each tier provides tax income each Winter, Settlement Wards that a Holding can fill, and a per-turn Muster limit of Retinues. The values per tier are below:\nSettlementTaxMusterWardsReachBuildNotesHamlet00311Natural holdings only; Placed at start of game Range 2 from capital.Village20005122Town400010244City600025366Metropolis800050488Capital only, requires Sovereign Industry (Titan of Industry)\nSettlement Wards\nA Settlement Ward is a slot inside a Settlement that holds one Holding; Wards are never placed on the map. A Settlement has one Ward per tier: a Village has 1, a Town 2, a City 3 and a Metropolis 4. A Hamlet has 3 Wards.\nChartering Settlements\nWhen chartering a new Settlement, place it in your Province, at least Range 4 from all other Settlements and Range 2 from any Outlaw Country. You can&#x27;t charter a Settlement on mountain or water Territory.\nSettlement Reach\nSettlements have a Reach value set by their tier, from 2 up to 8. Reach X determines which Territory you Control in your Province: at Reach 1 you Control all Territory within Range 1 o"}, {"title": "Infrastructure", "url": "rules-infrastructure.html", "text": "Infrastructure\nInfrastructure is the foundation of your Settlements. Each active Infrastructure provides an effect that applies to your entire empire and all its Settlements.\nExample: Wooden Walls protect all Settlements from Bandits and Raze actions, and a Cathedral raises your innate Faith by 2 each turn, regardless of how many Settlements you have.\nInfrastructure comes in 5 ascending tiers. Primitive Infrastructure builds the basic blocks of your empire. Developed Infrastructure expands and replaces some Primitive Infrastructure. Sophisticated Infrastructure allows more powerful effects and helps unlock unique Monument Holdings. Prodigious Infrastructure comes next, and Wondrous Infrastructure \u2014 the world Wonders \u2014 is the highest tier.\nTo build any Infrastructure, you need at least one active Infrastructure of the tier below it \u2014 so Developed needs one Primitive, Sophisticated needs one Developed (and therefore one Primitive), and so on up to Wondrous. One Tier Primitive means any one Primitive Infrastructure. Some Infrastructure also names its own requirement on top of this: a Library needs a Town Hall, and a Cathedral needs a Capital City \u2014 so a Cathedral needs one Primitive, "}, {"title": "Territory & Terrain", "url": "rules-territory-terrain.html", "text": "Territory &amp; Terrain\nTerritory is the smallest unit of land. To move from one Territory to another, you move Range 1. To be within a Territory is Range 0; adjacent is Range 1; next to is Range 2.\nSpeed X \u2014 An Army&#x27;s movement range in Territories per Move action. Base Speed value of an army is Speed 5\nTerritories carry modifiers by hex type (grassland, forest, barrens, wetlands, water, mountain), and are Uncontrolled, Contested, or Controlled. Territory begins Uncontrolled. By chartering Settlements you Control Territories: each Settlement&#x27;s Reach X adds every Territory within that Range to your Province. If another player&#x27;s Settlement Reach reaches any Territory you Control, that Territory is Contested.\nTo border another player, your Reach must be within or adjacent to their Territory.\nTerrainMap EffectRaw MaterialsBattle EffectGrassland\u2014Arable Land, ApiaryHill: An army on a Hill Seizes the Initiative every Skirmish.  Open Field: Ranged Weapons gain +1 to Strike.WetlandsSpeed \u22121 per Territory moved throughPeat Bog, ForestryMire: Gain Unwieldy and Immune Steady; \u22121 to Save.Barrensgain StrainedQuarry, Salt WorksGain Strained.MountainsImpassableMine, QuarryImpassable"}, {"title": "Public Order", "url": "rules-public-order.html", "text": "Public Order\nFaith and Doubt adjust your Public Order the moment they&#x27;re generated \u2014 each Faith raises it by 1, each Doubt lowers it by 1, applied immediately. Public Order is capped between \u22125 and 10, and your current band&#x27;s effects (below) are always active at your current value. A band&#x27;s X is its value in the current Era (the Era columns of the table).\nFirst Doubt of the turn. Some effects (e.g. Reliquary Sanctum, Episcopal Court) reduce the first Doubt (or first two) you gain each turn, from any source \u2014 each instance of Doubt uses up one reduction. Because Doubt applies immediately, this is whichever Doubt lands first in the turn \u2014 usually your innate modifiers in the Empire Phase, but it can be an opponent&#x27;s action if that resolves first. Track whether you&#x27;ve taken Doubt yet this turn; the marker resets at the Start of each Empire Phase, before innate modifiers apply.\nYour innate Public Order modifiers (below) are checked once each turn during the Empire Phase and applied like any other Faith / Doubt.\nPOStateEffectX: FoundingX: AscensionX: EminenceX: Zenith-5UprisingSpawn X Bandit Camp(s) in your Outlaw Country1234-4RecessionTax Income -X per Settleme"}, {"title": "Treasury & Upkeep", "url": "rules-treasury-upkeep.html", "text": "Treasury &amp; Upkeep\nYour Treasury is the gold you Control. Each Empire Phase you gain your Revenue (tax, trade, and Holding income) and pay your Upkeep (Armies, Holdings, and Infrastructure); the net lands in your Treasury. Costs you pay during the turn come out of the same Treasury.\nHolding upkeep and Build Timer follow the Holding&#x27;s Standing requirement \u2014 by Standing: Untested 100 (Build Timer 1), Rising 200 (Build Timer 2), Established 300 (Build Timer 3), Sovereign 400 (Build Timer 4); Natural 0. Holdings and Infrastructure only pay upkeep while active: none while being built, Damaged, or under repair.\nArmy upkeep = the sum of each Army&#x27;s cost (by Retinue type) \u2212 Upkeep modifiers. Army costs by Retinue type: Levy 1000, Man-at-Arms 2000, Sergeant 3000, Oathsworn 3000.\nTracking tip: keep three small piles \u2014 Treasury, Revenue, Upkeep. When you build something with income or upkeep, add it to the matching pile; when it&#x27;s Damaged or an Army is disbanded, subtract it. Each turn it&#x27;s just Treasury + Revenue \u2212 Upkeep, with no recounting.\nInsolvency &amp; Bankruptcy\nThis is an exception path \u2014 skip it until it happens.\nYou go Insolvent the moment your Treasury can&"}, {"title": "Trade & Income", "url": "rules-trade-income.html", "text": "Trade &amp; Income\nWho Can Trade\nWho can trade: a player needs a signed Trade Agreement and either active Dirt Roads or a Can Trade effect (e.g. Harbor).\nCraft X: Craft Holdings count toward how much income your Trade Agreements generate \u2014 any effect that grants Craft +X.\nTrade income: for each active Trade Agreement, both players gain gold equal to 100 \u00d7 the Host&#x27;s Craft X.\nWhen income flows:\n\nWhen you sign a Trade Agreement: the player who did not perform the Sign Treaty action gets trade income the next time they&#x27;re Host. Afterwards, both get trade income each turn either of them is Host.\nWhen you end a Trade Agreement: the player who ended it gets trade income the next time they&#x27;re Host, then trading ceases.\n\nRuleValueIncome per Craft100RequirementsA signed Trade Agreement, and each player has active Dirt Roads or a Can Trade effect (e.g. Harbor, Shipyard)No-trade SeasonSpring\nIncome Types\n\nTaxes: each Winter, in the Income &amp; Upkeep step of the Empire Phase, gain tax income from each of your Settlements by tier, after modifiers.\nTrade: see above.\nHoldings: gain Holding income in the Income &amp; Upkeep step of the Empire Phase.\n\nGlossary \u00b7 Economy &amp; Publi"}, {"title": "Armies", "url": "rules-armies.html", "text": "Armies\nArmies Overview\nArmies are collections of Retinues on the Realm, and are the target of Move actions. An Army holds up to 25 Retinues and up to a single piece of equipment of each type (armor, weapon, shield, and Retinue). Armies cost upkeep each Empire Phase (see Treasury &amp; Upkeep).\nWhile an Army is engaged in a Battle or Lay Siege action started by another player&#x27;s Army, neither Army can be the target of any actions until that Battle or Lay Siege resolves.\nMustering\nArmies are raised and reinforced with the Muster action (see Prowess Actions).\nDuring the Income &amp; Upkeep step, while an Army is within Range 0 of a Settlement you Control, you may change that Army&#x27;s equipment to any unlocked equipment.\nRetinue types \u2014 cost, to-Strike, and base profile:\nRetinueCostTo StrikeEnduranceMoraleSpeedMax SizeKeywordLevy10006+37+525\u2014Man-at-Arms20005+46+525\u2014Sergeant30003+35+525\u2014Oathsworn30004+34+525\u2014\nBlocked Armies\nA Blocked Army has Initiative \u22121 in the first Skirmish and can&#x27;t perform Move actions. An Army gains Blocked while it&#x27;s within a Settlement under Siege, or when it&#x27;s selected as the result of a condemned Prowess Envoy.\nGlossary \u00b7 Army StatesTerm"}, {"title": "Battle Phase", "url": "rules-battle-phase.html", "text": "Battle Phase\nA Battle is fought as a series of Skirmishes, run through the steps below until one side is wiped out, Routs, or successfully Falls Back. Full keyword detail is in the glossary tables at the end of this section.\nBeginning a Battle\n\nDeclare Army \u2014 declare which Army will Skirmish (if more than one is adjacent to either Army in the Battle).\n\n\nSeize the Initiative \u2014 the player who performed the Battle action usually gains Seize the Initiative, but Terrain and the Ministry of Military Strategy can change that. That player gains Initiative +1 in the first Skirmish.\n\nThe Skirmish Steps\n\nForm the line. Each side places up to 10 Retinues in its front line \u2014 one Strike die each \u2014 and may keep up to 5 in reserve to replace losses as they fall. An Army of 25 keeps the remainder in camp; between Skirmishes, camp and reserves refill the front line and reserve to their maximums.\n\n\nChoose Tactics and equipment. Both players secretly pick one Tactic and, if they have a choice, the equipment they&#x27;ll use this Skirmish (a Tiltyard Army picks its Ranged or Melee weapon; a Bastard Sword picks its 1H or 2H profile), then reveal together. A One-Shot weapon must be Equipped in the first "}, {"title": "Siege Warfare", "url": "rules-siege-warfare.html", "text": "Siege Warfare\n\nWhen you Lay Siege during the Envoy Phase, track the relevant Siege Timer(s).\nWhen a Siege Timer reaches 0, resolve the Siege before the Rest Phase: negotiate, then Battle if needed, then Capture or Sack.\n\nSiege Timer\nA Siege Timer is the sum of the besieged Settlement&#x27;s defenses minus the attacker&#x27;s Siege effects, to a minimum of 1 (no maximum). Every source below stacks \u2014 Wooden Walls (+1) and Stone Walls (+1) both count.\nSourceTimerNoteSettlement Size+0 to +4settlement tier (Hamlet 0 \u2026 Metropolis 4)Wooden Walls+1InfrastructureStone Walls+1InfrastructureCitadel+3HoldingGarrison+1InfrastructureStanding Army+1Army within Range 0 of the SettlementOffice of Works+2HoldingKeep+1InfrastructureFortress of Faith+3Heritage; While your Public Order is 3 or higherAttacker effects\u2212 variesOrdnance Yard \u22122, Colossus \u22122, Siege Camp \u22121, Siege Works \u22121\nBeginning a Siege\n\nEnd a Move action with your Army adjacent to another player&#x27;s Settlement you&#x27;re At War with.\n\n\nYour Army must stay there for the Siege Timer and can&#x27;t take other actions.\n\n\nIf you&#x27;re attacked while sieging and you Fall Back, the Siege is broken and the Siege Timer is removed from play."}, {"title": "Bandits", "url": "rules-bandits.html", "text": "Bandits\nOutlaw Country\nOutlaw Country is zones of Territory no player can Control, where Bandit Camps spawn. Setup places zones in two ways; after Setup, every zone works the same.\n\nYour zone (Deploy): demarcate 3 Territories in your starting region, each within Range 1 of at least one other Outlaw Country Territory and at least Range 2 from any Settlement \u2014 the first exactly Range 2 from your Town, and none within Range 2 of your Hamlet. If that&#x27;s not possible, place them Range 2 from your capital Settlement.\nWild zones (last Setup step): the Host scatters more zones over the unclaimed board \u2014 the number of players \u00f7 2, rounded down, + 1. Each is 3 connected Territories, none on mountain or water Territory, at least Range 3 from every player&#x27;s Province and at least Range 5 from every other Outlaw Country zone. Each Province starts the game with exactly one Outlaw Country zone.\n\nA zone is your Outlaw Country while any of its Territories is within your Province. A zone in no player&#x27;s Province belongs to no one: its camps spawn and grow, but take no action until they&#x27;re within a player&#x27;s Province; a camp that grows into a Bandit Army Marches like any other.\nS"}, {"title": "Holdings", "url": "rules-holdings.html", "text": "Holdings\nHoldings are listed by the Standing they require, Domain by Domain; Monuments are marked (Monument). A Holding that requires two Standings appears under both.\nNo RequirementHoldingInfrastructure ReqMastery ChainEffectAlchemy\u2014Peat Bog+500; Craft +2Animal Husbandry\u2014Arable LandNatural, Unlock Crude armor and shield. Upkeep \u2212500Apiary\u2014\u2014+500; Natural; Craft +1Apothecary\u2014Alchemy+500; Gain Heal 8, or improve Heal by +1.Arable Land\u2014Hamlet+500; Natural; Craft +1Bakery\u2014MeaderyNatural; Faith +1; +1000; Craft +2Burgages\u2014WorkyardNatural; Faith +1Butchery\u2014Salt Works, Charcoal BurnerNatural; +500; Upkeep \u2212500; Craft +1Caravanery\u2014Saddlery, StableNatural; Authority \u22122 to Intercept Caravan actions targeting your settlements; Craft +2; Speed \u22122 to non-allied armies in your Province.Carpentry\u2014ForestryBuild Timer \u22121; +500; Craft +1Census Hall\u2014BurgagesNatural; Doubt +1; +1000Chandlery\u2014ApiaryCraft +1; Authority \u22121 to Cunning actions targeting youCommon Land\u2014Hamlet+1000; Natural, Doubt +1Courier Network\u2014InnOnce per Envoy Phase before voting: Authority \u22121 on Target Envoy; Once per Envoy Phase: select a Personal Action you performed this turn. Next turn, you may perform that action in the Empire Ph"}, {"title": "Melee Weapons", "url": "rules-melee-weapons.html", "text": "Melee Weapons\nWeaponTierAPInitKeywordsFarm ToolCrude0+0AwkwardCudgelCrude\u22121\u221212H, Unwieldy, AwkwardPitchforkCrude0+12H, Unwieldy, AwkwardDaggersCast0+02H, Deadly, AwkwardShort SwordCast0+0SteadySpearCast\u22121+1UnwieldyArming SwordWrought\u22121+0SteadyPikeWrought\u22122+12H, Steady, Unwieldy, Deadly, AwkwardFlailWrought\u22121+0Unwieldy, Unstoppable, Cleave, AwkwardHalberdWrought\u22122+02H, SteadyBattle AxeWrought\u22123\u221212H, Unstoppable, Cleave, Negate ShieldedCavalry SpearWrought\u22122+1Steady, Unwieldy, Unstoppable, AwkwardMorningstarForged\u22124\u22121Cleave, Destroy ShieldBastard SwordForged\u22122+0Steady2HBastardForged\u22122+02H, Unstoppable, CleaveWar HammerForged\u221210\u221212H, Steady, Unstoppable, Negate Shielded, Destroy ShieldLanceForged\u22124+1Steady, Unwieldy, Unstoppable, Awkward, Destroy ShieldEstocTempered\u22123+0Steady, Deadly, UnstoppablePoleaxeTempered\u22125+02H, Steady, Cleave, Unstoppable, Negate Shielded"}, {"title": "Ranged Weapons", "url": "rules-ranged-weapons.html", "text": "Ranged Weapons\nRanged WeaponTierAPInitKeywordsHunting BowCrude0+22H, Unstoppable, AwkwardLongbowCast\u22121+22H, Unstoppable, Deadly, AwkwardThrowing AxeWrought\u22122+1Steady, Deadly, Unstoppable, Negate Shielded, Destroy Shield, One-Shot, AwkwardCrossbowForged\u22124+12H, Unwieldy, Deadly, Unstoppable, Negate Shielded, AwkwardThrowing SpearTempered\u22125+1Steady, Deadly, Unstoppable, Negate Shielded, Destroy Shield, One-Shot, AwkwardArquebusGunpowder\u22126+22H, Unwieldy, Unstoppable, Negate Shielded, Awkward"}, {"title": "Shields", "url": "rules-shields.html", "text": "Shields\nShieldTierSave BonusInitKeywordsNone\u2014+0+0\u2014Buckler ShieldCrude+1+0\u2014Targe ShieldCast+1+0Unwieldy, ShieldedKite ShieldWrought+1+0Steady, ShieldedTower ShieldForged+2+0Unwieldy, ShieldedHeater ShieldTempered+2+0Shielded, Immune Destroy Shield"}, {"title": "Armor", "url": "rules-armor.html", "text": "Armor\nArmorTierSaveKeywordsClothNone10+\u2014PaddedCrude8+\u2014LeatherCast7+\u2014ChainmailWrought6+\u2014Full PlateForged5+\u2014Gothic PlateTempered4+\u2014\nGlossary \u00b7 Equipment TiersTermDefinitionCrudeCrude equipment tier. Weapons: Farm Tool, Cudgel, Pitchfork; Ranged: Hunting Bow; Armor: Padded; Shield: Buckler Shield. Unlocked by: Animal Husbandry (armor &amp; shield).Crude WeaponsCrude-tier weapons: Farm Tool, Cudgel, Pitchfork, Hunting Bow.Crude ArmorCrude-tier armor: Padded. Unlocked by: Animal Husbandry.Crude ShieldsCrude-tier shields: Buckler Shield. Unlocked by: Animal Husbandry.CastCast equipment tier. Weapons: Daggers, Short Sword, Spear; Ranged: Longbow; Armor: Leather; Shield: Targe Shield. Unlocked by: Tannery (armor &amp; shield), Furnace (weapons).Cast WeaponsCast-tier weapons: Daggers, Short Sword, Spear, Longbow. Unlocked by: Furnace.Cast ArmorCast-tier armor: Leather. Unlocked by: Tannery.Cast ShieldsCast-tier shields: Targe Shield. Unlocked by: Tannery.WroughtWrought equipment tier. Weapons: Arming Sword, Pike, Flail, Halberd, Battle Axe, Cavalry Spear; Ranged: Throwing Axe; Armor: Chainmail; Shield: Kite Shield. Unlocked by: Blacksmith (weapons), Armory (armor &amp; shield).Wrought Weapo"}, {"title": "Factions", "url": "rules-factions.html", "text": "Heritages\nHeritageFeelDifficultyStrengthMechanicSiege SpecialistsOffensive, ArrogantLowMediumYou begin the game with a Siege Works (no Ward, Natural).HorsemastersFastLowMediumYou begin the game with a Stable (no Ward, Natural).Friends in Low PlacesScrappyHighHighYou begin the game with a Smuggler&#x27;s Nook (no Ward, Natural). At the Start of the Empire Phase, you may control one Bandit Camp outside your Territory. When a Bandit Camp is spawned, you may place it in your Outlaw Country instead. You cannot Build Holdings which require Piety or Prowess Standing.The MonarchSovereign VoiceLowMediumEach Council Phase, you choose every Council Envoy&#x27;s Domain. You abstain every Personal Envoy.Uncharted Sea LanesPirate LifeLowMediumOther players can&#x27;t perform Intercept Caravan on you. You begin the game with a Shipyard (no Ward, Natural).Royal MarriageDiplomatic, InescapableLowMediumOnce per game, you may join an Alliance without unanimous consent, or form one with a player who isn&#x27;t in an Alliance. While in that Alliance, each member gains Faith +1 and Influence +1 each Empire Phase.Patient CourtPatient &amp; ReservedLowMediumYour unspent Influence isn&#x27;t discarded in t"}, {"title": "Index", "url": "rules-index.html", "text": "Index\n"}, {"title": "Carpentry", "url": "type-arms.html#carpentry", "text": "Carpentry Arms Build Timer -1; +500; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Fletchery", "url": "type-arms.html#fletchery", "text": "Fletchery Arms Unlocks Ranged Weapons; Upkeep -500 "}, {"title": "Tannery", "url": "type-arms.html#tannery", "text": "Tannery Arms Natural; Unlocks Cast armor & shield. Upkeep -500; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Joinery", "url": "type-arms.html#joinery", "text": "Joinery Arms unlocks Shields; Upkeep -500 "}, {"title": "Furnace", "url": "type-arms.html#furnace", "text": "Furnace Arms Unlocks Cast Weapons; +500 "}, {"title": "Blacksmith", "url": "type-arms.html#blacksmith", "text": "Blacksmith Arms Craft +1; +500; Unlocks Wrought Weapons "}, {"title": "Armory", "url": "type-arms.html#armory", "text": "Armory Arms Unlock Wrought armor & shield; Upkeep -500; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Master Workshop", "url": "type-arms.html#master-workshop", "text": "Master Workshop Arms Upkeep -500; Craft +1; Add Serrated to Weapons "}, {"title": "Gilded Foundry", "url": "type-arms.html#gilded-foundry", "text": "Gilded Foundry Arms Upkeep -500; Unlock Forged armor & shield. "}, {"title": "Stable", "url": "type-arms.html#stable", "text": "Stable Arms Speed +1; Natural; Unlocks Cavalry Spear (Still requires Tier Unlock) "}, {"title": "Forge", "url": "type-arms.html#forge", "text": "Forge Arms Craft +2; Unlocks Forged Tier Weapons "}, {"title": "Tiltyard", "url": "type-arms.html#tiltyard", "text": "Tiltyard Arms Armies may be equipped with a Ranged and a Melee Weapon simultaneously; In addition, armies may equip two of the same 1H Melee Weapon to gain Dual Wield. "}, {"title": "Court Armoury", "url": "type-arms.html#court-armoury", "text": "Court Armoury Arms Planishing: Your to-Save can't be reduced beyond 10+. Upkeep -500; Crafted Armor & Shield Unlocked "}, {"title": "Butchery", "url": "type-logistics.html#butchery", "text": "Butchery Logistics Natural; +500; Upkeep -500; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Smokehouse", "url": "type-logistics.html#smokehouse", "text": "Smokehouse Logistics Natural; Craft +2; Upkeep -500 "}, {"title": "Caravanery", "url": "type-logistics.html#caravanery", "text": "Caravanery Logistics Natural; Authority -2 to Intercept Caravan actions targeting your settlements; Craft +2; Speed -2 to non-allied armies in your Province. "}, {"title": "Coliseum", "url": "type-logistics.html#coliseum", "text": "Coliseum Logistics Faith +1 while at War; Unlocks Man-at-Arms for Muster "}, {"title": "Conditioning Field", "url": "type-logistics.html#conditioning-field", "text": "Conditioning Field Logistics Faith +1 while not at War; Armies gain Nimble "}, {"title": "Grand Tournament", "url": "type-logistics.html#grand-tournament", "text": "Grand Tournament Logistics Reach +1, 3x per Envoy Phase: exchange 500 gold for Influence +1; Armies gain Riposte & Improve Parry by +1. "}, {"title": "Charcoal Burner", "url": "type-logistics.html#charcoal-burner", "text": "Charcoal Burner Logistics Natural; +500 "}, {"title": "Kiln", "url": "type-logistics.html#kiln", "text": "Kiln Logistics Natural; +500 "}, {"title": "Levy Hall", "url": "type-logistics.html#levy-hall", "text": "Levy Hall Logistics Natural, Speed +1; Upkeep -2000 while an Army is within Range 0 of a Settlement you Control "}, {"title": "Siege Camp", "url": "type-logistics.html#siege-camp", "text": "Siege Camp Logistics Siege Timer -1; Armies gain Immune Strained during Lay Siege "}, {"title": "Siege Works", "url": "type-logistics.html#siege-works", "text": "Siege Works Logistics Siege Timer -1; Siege Timers count down in Winter "}, {"title": "Battery Park", "url": "type-logistics.html#battery-park", "text": "Battery Park Logistics Your Siege Timers increment twice each turn. "}, {"title": "War College", "url": "type-logistics.html#war-college", "text": "War College Logistics Gain Influence +2 while At War; Unlocks Sergeants for Muster "}, {"title": "Masonry", "url": "type-works.html#masonry", "text": "Masonry Works No Upkeep on Primitive Infrastructure; Build Timer -1 "}, {"title": "Workyard", "url": "type-works.html#workyard", "text": "Workyard Works Natural; Doubt +1; +1000 "}, {"title": "Storehouse", "url": "type-works.html#storehouse", "text": "Storehouse Works Natural; Doubt +1; +2000; Build Timer -1 "}, {"title": "Census Hall", "url": "type-works.html#census-hall", "text": "Census Hall Works Natural; Doubt +1; +1000 "}, {"title": "Granary", "url": "type-works.html#granary", "text": "Granary Works Upkeep -500; Armies and Garrisons within controlled Settlements gain Immune Strained. "}, {"title": "Supply Depot", "url": "type-works.html#supply-depot", "text": "Supply Depot Works Craft +2; May Muster an Army in a Settlement under Siege and its Muster Timers count down. "}, {"title": "Trade Guild", "url": "type-works.html#trade-guild", "text": "Trade Guild Works No Upkeep on Developed Infrastructure; Build Timer -1 "}, {"title": "College of Engineering", "url": "type-works.html#college-of-engineering", "text": "College of Engineering Works No Upkeep on Sophisticated Infrastructure; Build Timer -1 "}, {"title": "Masons' Guild", "url": "type-works.html#masons-guild", "text": "Masons' Guild Works No Upkeep on Prodigious Infrastructure; Build Timer -2 "}, {"title": "Burgages", "url": "type-works.html#burgages", "text": "Burgages Works Natural; Faith +1 "}, {"title": "Citadel", "url": "type-works.html#citadel", "text": "Citadel Works Siege Timer +3, Controlled Settlements gain Reach +1 "}, {"title": "Castle Hall", "url": "type-works.html#castle-hall", "text": "Castle Hall Works Doubt +1; Upkeep -500; Tax Income is Doubled. "}, {"title": "Alchemy", "url": "type-commerce.html#alchemy", "text": "Alchemy Commerce +500; Craft +2 "}, {"title": "Weavery", "url": "type-commerce.html#weavery", "text": "Weavery Commerce +2000; Craft +2 "}, {"title": "Jewelry Foundry", "url": "type-commerce.html#jewelry-foundry", "text": "Jewelry Foundry Commerce +2000; Authority +1 to Cunning actions targeting this player; Craft +5 "}, {"title": "Market Square", "url": "type-commerce.html#market-square", "text": "Market Square Commerce Craft +2; +500 "}, {"title": "Spice Merchant", "url": "type-commerce.html#spice-merchant", "text": "Spice Merchant Commerce Natural; +1000; Authority +1 to Cunning actions targeting you; Craft +4 "}, {"title": "Harbor", "url": "type-commerce.html#harbor", "text": "Harbor Commerce Craft +2; Can Trade; Extort 500 per player without Harbor "}, {"title": "Merchant Quarter", "url": "type-commerce.html#merchant-quarter", "text": "Merchant Quarter Commerce +1000; Craft +3; Trade Partners gain Craft +2 "}, {"title": "Money Lending", "url": "type-commerce.html#money-lending", "text": "Money Lending Commerce Extort 1000; Once per turn, you may loan money to Trade Partners at 100 per 1000/turn interest (minimum 100); on Default: Perform Demand Tribute "}, {"title": "Shipyard", "url": "type-commerce.html#shipyard", "text": "Shipyard Commerce Craft +4; Can Trade; Water Territory treated as Grassland for movement "}, {"title": "Courtyard", "url": "type-commerce.html#courtyard", "text": "Courtyard Commerce Craft +1; Faith +1 "}, {"title": "Artisan Workshop", "url": "type-commerce.html#artisan-workshop", "text": "Artisan Workshop Commerce +1000; Faith +1 "}, {"title": "Court Artists", "url": "type-commerce.html#court-artists", "text": "Court Artists Commerce Extort 500 twice; Targets of Extort from Court Artist gain Faith +1 "}, {"title": "Emporium", "url": "type-commerce.html#emporium", "text": "Emporium Commerce +1000; Players who trade with you gain Craft +3 "}, {"title": "Chandlery", "url": "type-devotion.html#chandlery", "text": "Chandlery Devotion Craft +1; Authority -1 to Cunning actions targeting you "}, {"title": "Interrogation Chambers", "url": "type-devotion.html#interrogation-chambers", "text": "Interrogation Chambers Devotion Extort 500; Actions targeting this player that cause Doubt are reduced by 1, to a minimum of 0. "}, {"title": "Priory", "url": "type-devotion.html#priory", "text": "Priory Devotion Faith +2 "}, {"title": "Abbey", "url": "type-devotion.html#abbey", "text": "Abbey Devotion Faith +1; Authority -1 to Piety actions targeting you "}, {"title": "Reliquary", "url": "type-devotion.html#reliquary", "text": "Reliquary Devotion Faith +1; First two Doubt each Empire Phase reduced by 1 "}, {"title": "Monastery", "url": "type-devotion.html#monastery", "text": "Monastery Devotion Reach +1; Faith +1; Influence +1 "}, {"title": "Execution Dock", "url": "type-devotion.html#execution-dock", "text": "Execution Dock Devotion Authority -2 to Foster Rebellion actions targeting your settlements; Players who target you or your Settlements with actions that would cause Doubt before modifiers gain Doubt +1 "}, {"title": "Hospitaller", "url": "type-devotion.html#hospitaller", "text": "Hospitaller Devotion Recover improved by +1; Enduring: Successful Recovered rolls do not count towards the panic check threshold. "}, {"title": "Episcopal Court", "url": "type-devotion.html#episcopal-court", "text": "Episcopal Court Devotion Faith +1; Reduce the first instance of Doubt each Empire Phase by 1, min 0. "}, {"title": "Apothecary", "url": "type-devotion.html#apothecary", "text": "Apothecary Devotion +500; Gain Recover 8, or improve Recover by +1. "}, {"title": "Infirmary", "url": "type-devotion.html#infirmary", "text": "Infirmary Devotion +500; Improve Recover by +1 "}, {"title": "Pilgrimage Site", "url": "type-devotion.html#pilgrimage-site", "text": "Pilgrimage Site Devotion Faith +1; Extort 500 every player without a Pilgrimage Site; Doubt +1 to all other players without a Pilgrimage Site "}, {"title": "Unforgotten Shrine", "url": "type-devotion.html#unforgotten-shrine", "text": "Unforgotten Shrine Devotion When your Piety actions give their target Faith, it gains Faith +1 more; when they give Doubt, it gains Doubt +1 more. "}, {"title": "Inn", "url": "type-court.html#inn", "text": "Inn Court Faith +1 per Trade Partner with Craft 3+, and each of those partners gains Faith +1; Influence +1 "}, {"title": "Jester's Court", "url": "type-court.html#jester-s-court", "text": "Jester's Court Court First and second Oppose on an Envoy of yours each Envoy Phase: reduce by 1 "}, {"title": "Bell Tower", "url": "type-court.html#bell-tower", "text": "Bell Tower Court Influence +1 each Empire Phase; Authority +1 to envoys sent during the Council Phase. "}, {"title": "Embassy", "url": "type-court.html#embassy", "text": "Embassy Court Diplomacy Envoys cannot Fail; Other non-vassal players gain Faith +1 per Signed Treaty with you besides Peace. "}, {"title": "Academy", "url": "type-court.html#academy", "text": "Academy Court Authority +1 to Council Envoys; gain Influence +1 each Empire Phase "}, {"title": "University", "url": "type-court.html#university", "text": "University Court May spend one additional Influence per Support or Oppose; Influence +1 per Domain you are Rising "}, {"title": "Courier Network", "url": "type-court.html#courier-network", "text": "Courier Network Court Once per Envoy Phase before voting: Authority -1 on Target Envoy; Once per Envoy Phase: select a Personal Action you performed this turn. Next turn, you may perform that action in the Empire Phase, but you send 1 fewer Envoy next turn. "}, {"title": "Toll House", "url": "type-secrecy.html#toll-house", "text": "Toll House Secrecy Natural, Extort 2000 when non-Allied Army ends a Move action within your Province; Once per turn: when an Army ends a Move action within your Province, Perform a Diplomacy action targeting that army's player "}, {"title": "Secret Cellar", "url": "type-secrecy.html#secret-cellar", "text": "Secret Cellar Secrecy Natural; Passed Cunning envoys Recoup 500 Gold; Endorsed Cunning envoys Recoup 1000 Gold "}, {"title": "Smuggler's Nook", "url": "type-secrecy.html#smuggler-s-nook", "text": "Smuggler's Nook Secrecy gain Immune Uprising (Bandit Camp Spawn at -5PO); Bandit Camps in your Outlaw Country don't target you and instead target other players randomly. "}, {"title": "Syndicate Hub", "url": "type-secrecy.html#syndicate-hub", "text": "Syndicate Hub Secrecy Whenever a Bandit Camp within your Province Extorts, you Extort the Bandit Camp for half the amount. "}, {"title": "Black Market", "url": "type-secrecy.html#black-market", "text": "Black Market Secrecy When another player Extorts gold from any source: Extort 200 per 1000 (minimum 100) from that player at the end of that resolution. When another player Recoups gold from any source: Extort 200 per 1000 (minimum 100) from that player at the end of that resolution. "}, {"title": "Forgery Workshop", "url": "type-secrecy.html#forgery-workshop", "text": "Forgery Workshop Secrecy Extort 300 anytime a player Opposes an Envoy of yours; Once per Envoy Phase: attempt another Cunning Envoy if your Cunning Envoy Failed. If it Passes or is Endorsed, it must target a different player. "}, {"title": "Toxicarium", "url": "type-secrecy.html#toxicarium", "text": "Toxicarium Secrecy Weapons gain Poison; Endorsed Cunning actions give an additional Doubt +1 to Target "}, {"title": "Charnel House", "url": "type-secrecy.html#charnel-house", "text": "Charnel House Secrecy Indecisive, Aimless, & Recession effects are doubled for all players "}, {"title": "Plague Pit", "url": "type-secrecy.html#plague-pit", "text": "Plague Pit Secrecy Cunning actions give an additional Doubt +1 to Target; No longer affected by all Public Order effects (positive or negative). This player cannot be the target of a Convert action. "}, {"title": "Beacon Towers", "url": "type-secrecy.html#beacon-towers", "text": "Beacon Towers Secrecy Natural; At the Start of the Empire Phase, you may select an Army within your Province and move it up to its modified Speed. Whenever a non-allied Army ends a Move action within your Province, you may immediately perform a Move action "}, {"title": "Forgotten Catacombs", "url": "type-secrecy.html#forgotten-catacombs", "text": "Forgotten Catacombs Secrecy Cunning actions targeting you can't be Endorsed "}, {"title": "Cipher Chamber", "url": "type-secrecy.html#cipher-chamber", "text": "Cipher Chamber Secrecy At the Start of the Empire Phase: select an army you did not select last turn; that army gains Blocked. At the Start of the Empire Phase: select any active Timer you did not select last turn; increase it by 2. "}, {"title": "Herb Garden", "url": "type-husbandry.html#herb-garden", "text": "Herb Garden Husbandry +1000; Natural; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Animal Husbandry", "url": "type-husbandry.html#animal-husbandry", "text": "Animal Husbandry Husbandry Natural, Unlock Crude armor and shield. Upkeep -500 "}, {"title": "Saddlery", "url": "type-husbandry.html#saddlery", "text": "Saddlery Husbandry +500; Natural; Speed +2; Unlocks Lance (Still requires Tier Unlock) "}, {"title": "Vineyard", "url": "type-husbandry.html#vineyard", "text": "Vineyard Husbandry +500; Natural; +1500 in Fall "}, {"title": "Orchard", "url": "type-husbandry.html#orchard", "text": "Orchard Husbandry +1500; Natural; +500 in Fall "}, {"title": "Bakery", "url": "type-husbandry.html#bakery", "text": "Bakery Husbandry Natural; Faith +1; +1000; Craft +2 "}, {"title": "Meadery", "url": "type-husbandry.html#meadery", "text": "Meadery Husbandry Natural; Faith +1; Speed +2 in Winter "}, {"title": "Winery", "url": "type-husbandry.html#winery", "text": "Winery Husbandry Natural; +800; Craft +3 "}, {"title": "Cidery", "url": "type-husbandry.html#cidery", "text": "Cidery Husbandry Natural; Faith +1; +800; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Mill", "url": "type-husbandry.html#mill", "text": "Mill Husbandry Natural; +1000 "}, {"title": "Quarry", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#quarry", "text": "Quarry Raw Materials +500; Natural; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Salt Works", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#salt-works", "text": "Salt Works Raw Materials +500; Natural; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Apiary", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#apiary", "text": "Apiary Raw Materials +500; Natural; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Peat Bog", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#peat-bog", "text": "Peat Bog Raw Materials +500; Natural; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Forestry", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#forestry", "text": "Forestry Raw Materials +500; Natural; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Fishmongery", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#fishmongery", "text": "Fishmongery Raw Materials +500; Natural; Craft +2 "}, {"title": "Mine", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#mine", "text": "Mine Raw Materials +500; Natural; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Arable Land", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#arable-land", "text": "Arable Land Raw Materials +500; Natural; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Common Land", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#common-land", "text": "Common Land Raw Materials +1000; Natural, Doubt +1 "}, {"title": "Ossuary Crypt", "url": "type-monument.html#ossuary-crypt", "text": "Ossuary Crypt Monument All player's Piety actions give an additional Doubt +1. You may target players with Piety actions regardless of your Public Order. "}, {"title": "Baggage Train", "url": "type-monument.html#baggage-train", "text": "Baggage Train Monument Natural; Armies do not pay Upkeep while in your Province. Upkeep -2000 while not in your Province. At the Start of the Empire Phase, you may perform a Move action. "}, {"title": "Office of Works", "url": "type-monument.html#office-of-works", "text": "Office of Works Monument Natural; Settlements & allied armies inside them are not affected by 'Settlements being Besieged' restrictions. Siege Timer +2; Build Timer -2 "}, {"title": "Royal Pavilion", "url": "type-monument.html#royal-pavilion", "text": "Royal Pavilion Monument Armies gain Immune Strained, Improve Parry by +1; Gain +1 to Strike. Deadly, & Cleave also trigger Focused Strikes on a natural 8+. "}, {"title": "Imperial Palace", "url": "type-monument.html#imperial-palace", "text": "Imperial Palace Monument Each Empire Phase, all non-allied players with a lower Prowess value gain Doubt +2. If your Envoy would fail, it passes instead. "}, {"title": "Artillery Park", "url": "type-monument.html#artillery-park", "text": "Artillery Park Monument Siege Timers ignore Wooden & Stone Walls. Unlocks Arquebus; Settlements you Siege can't Sally Forth. Siege Timer -2. "}, {"title": "Ministry of Military Strategy", "url": "type-monument.html#ministry-of-military-strategy", "text": "Ministry of Military Strategy Monument Always gains Seize the Initiative, and your opponent doesn't; max initiative is increased to 3; Gain Drilled. "}, {"title": "Thieves' Guild", "url": "type-monument.html#thieves-guild", "text": "Thieves' Guild Monument Whenever another player performs a Cunning action, you may recoup 1000 gold; Extort half of Trade Income from players who don't trade with you "}, {"title": "Senate Hall", "url": "type-monument.html#senate-hall", "text": "Senate Hall Monument Faith +1, gain Influence +1 per other player each Empire Phase; Once per Envoy Phase: before players vote on an Envoy you choose, you may Condemn it if it's an At War player's Envoy, or Endorse it if it's an Ally's Envoy "}, {"title": "Papal Palace", "url": "type-monument.html#papal-palace", "text": "Papal Palace Monument You no longer pay cost for Piety Envoys. Each Empire Phase, Tithe every other player with lower Piety, resolved in the Extort step. "}, {"title": "Inquisitorial Palace", "url": "type-monument.html#inquisitorial-palace", "text": "Inquisitorial Palace Monument Doubt 1; Unlocks Grand Vizier which uses your Piety Value instead of Cunning.; All player actions that cause Doubt are increased by 1.  "}, {"title": "Preceptory of the Knight's Templar", "url": "type-monument.html#preceptory-of-the-knight-s-templar", "text": "Preceptory of the Knight's Templar Monument Unlocks Knight's Templar for Muster; While a Sacred War is active, gain 3 Faith during each Empire Phase "}, {"title": "Exalted Basilica", "url": "type-monument.html#exalted-basilica", "text": "Exalted Basilica Monument At the Start of the Empire Phase, you may perform an Endorsed Spread Truth. "}, {"title": "Manor House", "url": "type-monument.html#manor-house", "text": "Manor House Monument Natural; Gain +200 gold for each active natural Holding. "}, {"title": "Aristocratic Court", "url": "type-monument.html#aristocratic-court", "text": "Aristocratic Court Monument Each Empire Phase, Extort 1000 from each non-allied player with a lower Treasury. Your Vote counts as 2 votes toward Domain selection during the Council Phase. "}, {"title": "Studium Generale", "url": "type-monument.html#studium-generale", "text": "Studium Generale Monument Influence +1 per Established Standing; May gain one Sovereign Domain effect without spending the Domain Points "}, {"title": "Outlaw Rookery", "url": "type-monument.html#outlaw-rookery", "text": "Outlaw Rookery Monument Both Bandit Camps & you have Authority +1 on Personal Cunning Envoys. Endorsed Foster Rebellion instead places Bandit Armies with 25 retinues. "}, {"title": "Advanced Blast Furnace", "url": "type-monument.html#advanced-blast-furnace", "text": "Advanced Blast Furnace Monument Upkeep -1000; Crafted Weapons Unlocked; Craft +3 "}, {"title": "Whispering Undercroft", "url": "type-monument.html#whispering-undercroft", "text": "Whispering Undercroft Monument You always vote last, after the Host. Once per Personal Envoy Phase when a player sends an Envoy: that player must declare the specific action & target they would Perform if the Envoy passes (including sub-Actions). If it passes, they must Perform that declared action at the declared target. "}, {"title": "Outrider Intercept Post", "url": "type-monument.html#outrider-intercept-post", "text": "Outrider Intercept Post Monument Natural; Every Skirmish, you may force your opponent to reveal their Tactic Card they selected before you select your own. "}, {"title": "Port Authority", "url": "type-monument.html#port-authority", "text": "Port Authority Monument Gain +100 per Craft "}, {"title": "Turn Sequence", "url": "turn-sequence.html", "text": "turn sequence empire council envoy battle rest phase order of play"}, {"title": "Dirt Roads", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#dirt-roads", "text": "Dirt Roads infrastructure Can Trade; If you start a Move action within your Province, gain Speed +1"}, {"title": "Hitching Post", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#hitching-post", "text": "Hitching Post infrastructure Craft +1"}, {"title": "Muster Field", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#muster-field", "text": "Muster Field infrastructure Can Muster"}, {"title": "Wooden Walls", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#wooden-walls", "text": "Wooden Walls infrastructure Authority -2 to Raze actions from players targeting your settlements. Authority -1 to Bandit Cunning actions targeting your settlements."}, {"title": "Stone Roads", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#stone-roads", "text": "Stone Roads infrastructure If you start a Move action within your Province, gain additional Speed +1"}, {"title": "Town Hall", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#town-hall", "text": "Town Hall infrastructure Influence +1 each Empire Phase"}, {"title": "Chapel", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#chapel", "text": "Chapel infrastructure Faith +1"}, {"title": "Garrison", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#garrison", "text": "Garrison infrastructure Local Armies form (10/15/25/50 by Settlement size). All Garrisons share Retinues & Equipment. Can't be targeted; may not Sally Forth while under Siege. Do not pay upkeep."}, {"title": "Stone Walls", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#stone-walls", "text": "Stone Walls infrastructure Authority -2 to Destabilize actions from players targeting your settlements. Authority -1 to Bandit Cunning actions targeting your settlements."}, {"title": "Bridges", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#bridges", "text": "Bridges infrastructure Armies cross Water Territory at full movement within your Province; Stone Roads may be built over Water"}, {"title": "Library", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#library", "text": "Library infrastructure Council Envoys you send are always Endorsed"}, {"title": "Road Wardens", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#road-wardens", "text": "Road Wardens infrastructure Authority -1 to Bandit Cunning & Prowess actions targeting your settlements or armies."}, {"title": "Magistrate's Hall", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#magistrate-s-hall", "text": "Magistrate's Hall infrastructure Gain Tax Income +1000 per Settlement."}, {"title": "Keep", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#keep", "text": "Keep infrastructure When you Muster, reduce the Muster Timer by 1 and immediately gain Retinues equal to the combined muster limit. Siege Timer +1."}, {"title": "Aqueducts", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#aqueducts", "text": "Aqueducts infrastructure Reach +1; Upkeep -500; Build Timer -1; Influence +1"}, {"title": "Cathedral", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#cathedral", "text": "Cathedral infrastructure Faith +2"}, {"title": "Colossus", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#colossus", "text": "Colossus infrastructure You may support your own Personal Prowess Envoys before other players vote. Speed +2; Siege Timer -2, & gain Immune Blunder."}, {"title": "The Grand Exchange", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#the-grand-exchange", "text": "The Grand Exchange infrastructure You count as Trading with an additional 2 players. In addition, whenever you generate Trade Income by trading with another player, you generate twice as much for yourself."}, {"title": "The Eternal Sepulchre", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#the-eternal-sepulchre", "text": "The Eternal Sepulchre infrastructure If your Public Order would ever be less than 5, set it to 5 instead. Your Settlements gain Reach +2."}, {"title": "High Chancery", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#high-chancery", "text": "High Chancery infrastructure Once per Envoy Phase, you may Endorse one Envoy Sent by yourself after voting."}, {"title": "Move", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Move Prowess action Move an Army up to its Speed in Territories. Then choose one: March \u2014 move up to 2\u00d7 Speed, lose 1 Endurance, take no other action; Battle \u2014 end adjacent to an at-war Army not in a Settlement, then begin a Battle; Lay Siege \u2014 end adjacent to an at-war Settlement, then begin a Siege."}, {"title": "Declare War", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Declare War Prowess action Choose a non-allied player you have no NAP or active truce with. You and that player are now At War, and any Trade Agreements between you end. If the target is in a Defensive Alliance, every member is now At War with you."}, {"title": "Pillage", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Pillage Prowess action Choose an army you control within Reach of an at-war player's Settlement without an active Siege Timer. While that army remains within Reach of that Settlement and does not Lay Siege, Battle, or March, it may Extort half of that Settlement's holding income in the Extort step. A Settlement may be Pillaged once per Empire Phase. Pillage ends if [war ends / army leaves Reach / Settlement is besieged]."}, {"title": "Muster", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Muster Prowess action Choose one: Raise \u2014 if you have fewer Armies than your Era allows, place a new Army within a Settlement under your Control; or Reinforce \u2014 choose an Army you control. The Army must be within range 2 of a Settlement you Control with an active Muster Field, and at least Range 2 from any non-allied Army unless it is within Range 0 of a Settlement you Control. Choose how many Retinues to recruit (an Army can't exceed 25) and set a Muster Timer equal to that number \u00f7 your combined muster limit, rounded up. Each turn the Muster Timer counts down, the Army gains Retinues up to your combined muster limit and you begin paying their upkeep. You may change the Army's Retinue type and equipment while an army has an active Muster Timer."}, {"title": "Demand Tribute", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Demand Tribute Prowess action Choose a non-allied player you have no NAP with, then negotiate terms. If the target agrees, sign a NAP or Alliance (the target picks among the offered terms). If the target refuses, or later fails to meet the terms, immediately Declare War on them."}, {"title": "Intercept Caravan", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Intercept Caravan Cunning action Choose a player. The next turn that player is Host, Extort their Trade Income. If they have no Trade Income that turn, instead Extort 100 per their Craft."}, {"title": "Foster Rebellion", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Foster Rebellion Cunning action Choose a player. At the next Bandit Mechanics step, place a Bandit Camp of 10 Retinues in their Outlaw Country."}, {"title": "Raze", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Raze Cunning action Choose another player's Settlement, then choose one active Holding, active Infrastructure, or active Build Timer in it: that target becomes Damaged, and its effects are inactive until Repaired. A Damaged Build Timer doesn't count down until Repaired. If an active Build Timer hasn't been completed, instead, increase the Timer by 2."}, {"title": "Destabilize", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Destabilize Cunning action Choose a player. In the next Winter phase, during the Extort step, Extort one settlement's tax income. Each settlement can only be Destabilized once per Winter."}, {"title": "Sabotage", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Sabotage Cunning action Choose an army, that army gains Blocked until the end of next turn."}, {"title": "Spread Truth", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Spread Truth Piety action Each non-allied player gains Doubt 1. Each allied player gains Faith 1."}, {"title": "Send Missionaries", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Send Missionaries Piety action Choose a target player or Alliance. If the target is outside your Alliance, each player in it gains Doubt 2. If the target is inside your Alliance, each other allied player gains Faith 2."}, {"title": "Tithe", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Tithe Piety action Choose a player. Extort 10% of their Treasury (round down to the nearest 100, minimum 0)."}, {"title": "Convert", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Convert Piety action Choose another player's closest non-capital Settlement; its Public Order must be -5 or lower. Lay Siege using only Settlement-type Siege modifiers (Settlement Size and Citadel) and set a Convert Timer. When it reaches 0, the Settlement joins your empire (see Capture)."}, {"title": "Sacred War", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Sacred War Piety action Declare War on a non-ally you have no NAP or truce with, then immediately perform a Move action with one of your Armies."}, {"title": "Improve", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Improve Industry action Choose one: Infrastructure \u2014 choose an unlocked, available Infrastructure and set a Build Timer equal to its build time; when it completes, the Infrastructure becomes active in every Settlement in your Province. Or Expand a Settlement one tier (Village to Town, Town to City, City to Metropolis), adding a Ward."}, {"title": "Repair", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Repair Industry action Choose a Damaged Holding or Infrastructure in a Settlement you control and set Repair Timer 2. When it reaches 0, choose one: Restore \u2014 reactivate it with all effects; Demolish \u2014 remove the Holding tile from your Empire Tableau."}, {"title": "Build", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Build Industry action Choose an inactive Settlement Ward you control, then choose a Holding with one complete line of its Mastery Chain under your control (and meet its other requirements) and set a Build Timer equal to its build time (usually 1). When it completes, place the Holding in an available Ward slot; its effect activates immediately."}, {"title": "Charter", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Charter Industry action Charter a new Village \u2014 on in-province non-water, non-mountain Territory, Range 4+ from any Settlement and Range 2+ from Outlaw Country."}, {"title": "Sign Treaty", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Sign Treaty Diplomacy action Ask players to agree, then choose one and both sign it: Peace Treaty \u2014 end the war, set Truce Timer 5; Trade Agreement \u2014 begin trading next turn; Non-Aggression Pact \u2014 no Declare War (ending it via End Treaty gives both Truce Timer 5); Alliance \u2014 join, form, or invite to a Defensive or Military Alliance."}, {"title": "Negotiate", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Negotiate Diplomacy action Propose terms to a target; they agree or refuse. Terms may include gold, Settlement ownership, Territory, signing or ending a Treaty, or promises (non-binding)."}, {"title": "End Treaty", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "End Treaty Diplomacy action Choose a target with whom you have an active Treaty and no active Truce Timer; remove that Treaty. The target doesn't need to agree."}, {"title": "Envoy Outcomes", "url": "envoy-outcomes-ref.html", "text": "envoy outcomes condemned failed passed endorsed net influence resolve domain"}, {"title": "Peace Treaty", "url": "treaties-ref.html", "text": "Peace Treaty treaty Ends war between the two players; sets Truce Timer 5."}, {"title": "Trade Agreement", "url": "treaties-ref.html", "text": "Trade Agreement treaty Begin trading (Trade Income flows from next turn). Requires bordering, and each player has active Dirt Roads or a Can Trade effect."}, {"title": "Non-Aggression Pact", "url": "treaties-ref.html", "text": "Non-Aggression Pact treaty Neither player may Declare War on the other. Ending it via End Treaty gives both a Truce Timer 5."}, {"title": "Military Alliance", "url": "treaties-ref.html", "text": "Military Alliance treaty Mutual offensive pact: if a member Declares War, all members Declare War on the target next turn (and send 1 fewer envoy)."}, {"title": "Defensive Alliance", "url": "treaties-ref.html", "text": "Defensive Alliance treaty Mutual defense: attacking one member puts all members at war with the attacker."}, {"title": "Sovereign Standing", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Sovereign Standing edict win Reach a Sovereign Standing (Domain value 10) in any Domain."}, {"title": "Monument", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Monument edict win Have a Monument holding."}, {"title": "Wonder", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Wonder edict win Improve Infrastructure via a Wonder."}, {"title": "Wealth", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Wealth edict win Hold 50,000 gold in your Treasury for five consecutive turns."}, {"title": "Vassalize", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Vassalize edict win Vassalize a rival player (control their capital with no other settlements/armies under them)."}, {"title": "Living Saints", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Living Saints edict win Sustain Public Order 10 (Living Saints) for five consecutive turns (Pious Timer)."}, {"title": "Last Alliance Standing", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Last Alliance Standing edict win Be the last alliance standing \u2014 the game-ending stop condition."}, {"title": "Economy Reference", "url": "economy-ref.html", "text": "upkeep costs pursuit army infrastructure tax trade 2000 gold (the envoy action; holding then costs upkeep by type each Empire Phase) Each Empire Phase: by Standing: Untested 100 (Build Timer 1), Rising 200 (Build Timer 2), Established 300 (Build Timer 3), Sovereign 400 (Build Timer 4); Natural 0 sum of each Army's cost (by Retinue type) - Upkeep -X modifiers Per-settlement (see INFRASTRUCTURE); Masonry removes Primitive, Trade Guild removes Developed, College of Engineering removes Sophisticated Raze the top-most Holding of each Ward; Extort 2000 per settlement tier; reduce settlement by 1 tier; the controller removes one Ward (sacker's choice) and its Holdings; Sack Timer 2 Winter tax by Settlement tier: Hamlet 0 / Village 2000 / Town 4000 / City 6000 / Metropolis 8000 100 x host's Craft X per active Trade Agreement 2000 gold (Intercept Caravan / Foster Rebellion / Raze / Destabilize / Sabotage) 2000 gold (Improve / Build / Charter); 0 gold (Repair) Doubt 1 (Spread Truth / Send Missionaries / Tithe / Convert / Sacred War) None (Move / Declare War / Pillage / Muster / Demand Tribute) None (Sign Treaty / Negotiate / End Treaty)"}, {"title": "Grassland", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Grassland terrain \u2014"}, {"title": "Wetlands", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Wetlands terrain Speed -1 per Territory moved through"}, {"title": "Tundra", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Tundra terrain gain Strained"}, {"title": "Mountains", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Mountains terrain Impassable"}, {"title": "Water", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Water terrain Must end move after moving over 1 Water Territory (must end on land)"}, {"title": "Forest", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Forest terrain Speed -1 per Territory moved through"}, {"title": "Hill", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Hill terrain Gains Seize the Initiative. Where Settlements can be chartered."}, {"title": "Terrain & Movement", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "terrain movement grassland wetland barrens tundra mountain water forest roads bridge"}, {"title": "Bandits", "url": "bandits-ref.html", "text": "bandits outlaw country camp army growth cunning raze destabilize"}, {"title": "Timers, Influence & PO", "url": "systems-ref.html", "text": "timers influence public order modifiers faith doubt border tension"}, {"title": "Settlements", "url": "settlements-ref.html", "text": "settlements hamlet village town city metropolis tax muster wards reach"}, {"title": "Eras", "url": "eras-ref.html", "text": "eras founding ascension eminence zenith renown army cap"}, {"title": "Public Order Track", "url": "public-order-ref.html", "text": "public order faith doubt uprising living saints"}, {"title": "Domain Board", "url": "domain-board-ref.html", "text": "domain board standing indomitable grand vizier influence"}, {"title": "Seasons", "url": "seasons-ref.html", "text": "seasons winter spring summer fall"}, {"title": "Equipment", "url": "equipment-ref.html", "text": "equipment retinues weapons ranged shields armor stats"}, {"title": "Reference Tables", "url": "reference-tables.html", "text": "bandits timers influence gain trade rules build timers tier unlock standing effects"}, {"title": "Tactic Matrix", "url": "tactic-matrix-ref.html", "text": "tactic matrix scout ambush flank charge fighting defensive formation fall back initiative"}, {"title": "Escalation Campaign", "url": "escalation.html", "text": "escalation campaign combat battle mode overview"}, {"title": "Escalation Battle Rules", "url": "escalation-rules.html", "text": "escalation battle rules setup turn sequence skirmish walkthrough victory points dice"}, {"title": "Escalation Combat Pursuits", "url": "escalation-pursuits.html", "text": "escalation combat pursuits industry prowess piety cunning ranks mastery monument"}, {"title": "Combat Keywords", "url": "keywords-ref.html", "text": "keywords deadly cleave poison parry riposte"}, {"title": "Unbreakable", "url": "glossary.html#unbreakable", "text": "Unbreakable Skips the Break check entirely while Fatigued: never rolls, never takes break casualties. BUT still Routs if the morale target climbs to ROUT_THR+ from accumulated Fatigue. Stands fully immune, then collapses all at once \u2014 and because it stays full-size up to the Rout, it loses MORE soldiers when it finally breaks than a unit that bled down gradually."}, {"title": "Unshakable", "url": "glossary.html#unshakable", "text": "Unshakable Caps the morale target at CAP_THR permanently. Still TAKES every Break and Panic check each Skirmish (keeps bleeding casualties at a CAP_THR+ roll), but the target can never reach ROUT_THR, so it NEVER Routs. Bends and bleeds forever, never shatters. Makes the `shaking` stat (and the Abbey bonus) irrelevant \u2014 it's capped regardless."}, {"title": "Rally", "url": "glossary.html#rally", "text": "Rally Auto-passes the FIRST Break check it is ever required to take in a battle (no roll, no casualties, no Rout); every Break check after is normal. One free crisis, then mortal. The only one of the four that keeps `shaking` a live dial \u2014 so it's the one that synergizes with lowering KT base shaking and stacking Abbey +1."}, {"title": "Zealot", "url": "glossary.html#zealot", "text": "Zealot Locks the morale target at base `shaking`, ignoring ALL modifiers: Fatigue tokens don't raise it, shake bonuses (Abbey) don't lower it. Takes checks every Skirmish at that fixed number, never escalates, never Routs. A fixed wall whose strength is entirely its base stat. Unlike Unshakable (caps at 6), Zealot pins at base \u2014 which can be better or worse than 6 \u2014 and deliberately ignores Abbey synergy."}, {"title": "Steady", "url": "glossary.html#steady", "text": "Steady Initiative cannot be reduced by Tactics."}, {"title": "Unwieldy", "url": "glossary.html#unwieldy", "text": "Unwieldy Initiative cannot be improved by Tactics."}, {"title": "2H", "url": "glossary.html#2h", "text": "2H Cannot use a Shield: while a 2H weapon is Equipped, your Shield gives nothing that Skirmish (no Save bonus, Initiative or keywords)."}, {"title": "Deadly", "url": "glossary.html#deadly", "text": "Deadly On a Focused Strike: that strike's AP is increased by 5, and the defender may Parry or Recover only with a Focused roll."}, {"title": "Unstoppable", "url": "glossary.html#unstoppable", "text": "Unstoppable -2 to the defender's Parry roll (to a maximum of 10+); a Parry against it can't Riposte."}, {"title": "Cleave", "url": "glossary.html#cleave", "text": "Cleave On a Focused Strike: roll one extra Strike die at your modified to-Strike."}, {"title": "Poison", "url": "glossary.html#poison", "text": "Poison When the Defender receives a Strike and rolls a Focused Save, it fails; the resulting wound may only be Recovered with a Focused Recover."}, {"title": "Nimble", "url": "glossary.html#nimble", "text": "Nimble Gain Initiative +1 in the first Skirmish of each Battle."}, {"title": "Drilled", "url": "glossary.html#drilled", "text": "Drilled Does not lose Endurance in the first Skirmish of each Battle."}, {"title": "Destroy Shield", "url": "glossary.html#destroy-shield", "text": "Destroy Shield On a Focused Strike: the target loses its Shield attributes for the rest of the Battle."}, {"title": "Blunder", "url": "glossary.html#blunder", "text": "Blunder At Initiative -2, your to-Strike is set to 10+, before other negative modifiers."}, {"title": "One-Shot", "url": "glossary.html#one-shot", "text": "One-Shot Must be Equipped in the first Skirmish of a Battle, and can't be Equipped after it. Requires a Tiltyard."}, {"title": "Parry", "url": "glossary.html#parry", "text": "Parry If your Army has gained Parry, roll a D10 to attempt to Parry a Strike before an Armor Save. On a 8+ (Improved by Improved Parry), the Strike is Parried and has no further effect."}, {"title": "Riposte", "url": "glossary.html#riposte", "text": "Riposte If your Army has gained Riposte and rolls a Focused Parry against a Melee Weapon's Strike, you Riposte: your opponent immediately takes a Strike from your melee weapon. You can Riposte a Riposte."}, {"title": "Awkward", "url": "glossary.html#awkward", "text": "Awkward While equipped with this weapon during a skirmish, you cannot Parry, and so cannot Riposte."}, {"title": "Recover", "url": "glossary.html#recover", "text": "Recover If your Army has gained Recover and a to-Save roll fails, roll a D10 & compare it to your Recover value: a result greater than or equal to your Recover value recovers the retinue. Recovered Strikes still count toward the Panic check threshold."}, {"title": "Enduring", "url": "glossary.html#enduring", "text": "Enduring Successfully Recovered Strikes don't count toward the Panic check threshold."}, {"title": "Serrated", "url": "glossary.html#serrated", "text": "Serrated A cumulative -2 penalty to the defender's Recover roll."}, {"title": "Planishing", "url": "glossary.html#planishing", "text": "Planishing A Focused Save succeeds, regardless of AP."}, {"title": "Fatigue Token", "url": "glossary.html#fatigue-token", "text": "Fatigue Token Each token reduces Morale by 2; if your modified Morale is ever 11+, your army Routs. Tokens stack."}, {"title": "Shielded", "url": "glossary.html#shielded", "text": "Shielded A cumulative -1 penalty to the Strike roll (to a maximum of 10+). Sources: a shield's -1 to Strike."}, {"title": "Dual Wield", "url": "glossary.html#dual-wield", "text": "Dual Wield A failed Strike is rerolled once; the rerolled Strike can be Focused. Dual Wield confers Two-Handed. You cannot reroll successful Strikes."}, {"title": "Immune [keyword]", "url": "glossary.html#immune-keyword", "text": "Immune [keyword] Can't gain that keyword's effect as it applies to your Army (e.g. Immune Strain, Destroy Shield, Steady, etc.)."}, {"title": "Negate [keyword]", "url": "glossary.html#negate-keyword", "text": "Negate [keyword] Your opponent can't gain that keyword's effect as it applies to their Army (e.g. Negate Shielded)."}, {"title": "AP", "url": "glossary.html#ap", "text": "AP Armor Penetration \u2014 a weapon's (negative) modifier to the defender's Save roll; the more negative, the harder to save."}, {"title": "Blocked", "url": "glossary.html#blocked", "text": "Blocked Initiative -1 in the first Skirmish (negated by Immune Blocked). Armies with Blocked cannot perform Move actions."}, {"title": "Strained", "url": "glossary.html#strained", "text": "Strained Initiative -1 every Skirmish (negated by Immune Strain). Does not gain Endurance in the Empire Phase."}, {"title": "Seize the Initiative", "url": "glossary.html#seize-the-initiative", "text": "Seize the Initiative Typically, the player who performed the Battle Action gains Seize the Initiative, but Terrain and the Ministry of Military Strategy can affect that. When a player gains Seize the Initiative, the player gains Initiative +1 in the first skirmish."}, {"title": "Attacker / Defender", "url": "glossary.html#attacker-defender", "text": "Attacker / Defender The Attacker performed the Move action that caused the Battle or Lay Siege; the other side is the Defender."}, {"title": "Battle", "url": "glossary.html#battle", "text": "Battle A collection of Skirmishes between two players, continuing until a side's Retinue count is reduced to 0, Routs, or successfully Falls Back, ending the Battle."}, {"title": "Skirmish", "url": "glossary.html#skirmish", "text": "Skirmish One round of a Battle, run through the numbered Battle steps; a Battle repeats Skirmishes until it ends."}, {"title": "Casualty", "url": "glossary.html#casualty", "text": "Casualty A retinue removed from the field \u2014 from an unsaved Strike or a failed Panic or Break check."}, {"title": "Field", "url": "glossary.html#field", "text": "Field Your retinues in play \u2014 front line (up to 10) plus reserve (up to 5). Casualties leave the field at once, lowering its count."}, {"title": "Endurance", "url": "glossary.html#endurance", "text": "Endurance A side's stamina. Each side that fights loses 1 per Skirmish; at 0 it becomes Fatigued."}, {"title": "Fatigued", "url": "glossary.html#fatigued", "text": "Fatigued A side at 0 Endurance. Each Skirmish its field takes a Break check, then it gains a Fatigue token."}, {"title": "Break check", "url": "glossary.html#break-check", "text": "Break check Taken by each Fatigued side's field every Skirmish, just before it gains its Fatigue token. Roll Morale (5 dice, modified by Fatigue tokens); failures are casualties, but a Break check never triggers a Panic check. Unbreakable auto-passes."}, {"title": "Panic check", "url": "glossary.html#panic-check", "text": "Panic check Taken at most once per Skirmish by a side that suffered more than 5 casualties in that Skirmish (Recovered Strikes count, unless Enduring), after both sides have Struck. Roll Morale (5 dice); Immune Panic auto-passes."}, {"title": "Morale", "url": "glossary.html#morale", "text": "Morale How steady a retinue is when tested (lower is steadier; see the retinue table). Break and Panic checks roll it: a D10 per retinue in the field, up to 5 dice, each must meet its modified value; failures are casualties. If the modified value is ever 11+, the army Routs."}, {"title": "Rout", "url": "glossary.html#rout", "text": "Rout The army breaks and leaves the Battle. Apply casualties equal to the remaining retinues. Whenever an army's modified Morale value reaches 11+ or more, it Routs automatically."}, {"title": "Fall Back", "url": "glossary.html#fall-back", "text": "Fall Back A controlled retreat that ends the Battle with at least one retinue left \u2014 a partial success."}, {"title": "Strike", "url": "glossary.html#strike", "text": "Strike A landed hit. Roll a D10, apply modifiers to the roll, and Strike on a result >= the to-Strike number. The target may then Parry, Save, and Recover."}, {"title": "to-Strike number", "url": "glossary.html#to-strike-number", "text": "to-Strike number The D10 result a retinue needs to Strike (see the retinue table; lower is better). Bonuses add to the roll; penalties and Fatigue tokens subtract."}, {"title": "Save", "url": "glossary.html#save", "text": "Save The defender's roll to avoid a casualty: roll a D10, add the weapon's AP (a negative) and the shield's Save bonus (a positive); the hit is saved on a result >= the armor value."}, {"title": "Natural roll", "url": "glossary.html#natural-roll", "text": "Natural roll The number on the die before any modifiers. Modifiers never change what counts as 'natural'."}, {"title": "Initiative", "url": "glossary.html#initiative", "text": "Initiative Decides who Strikes first each Skirmish (higher first). Runs -2 to +2 (Ministry can raise the maximum to +3). At -2 or lower you Blunder."}, {"title": "Tactic", "url": "glossary.html#tactic", "text": "Tactic A choice both players make secretly and reveal together each Skirmish; it can shift Initiative, Strike, and Save rolls."}, {"title": "Dual-equip", "url": "glossary.html#dual-equip", "text": "Dual-equip Carry two weapons at once (e.g. melee + ranged). Granted by the Tiltyard."}, {"title": "Monument", "url": "glossary.html#monument", "text": "Monument A Domain's capstone Holding. Completing one scores its Edict and grants a powerful effect."}, {"title": "Faith X", "url": "glossary.html#faith-x", "text": "Faith X Gain X Faith: each Faith raises your Public Order track by 1 when resolved."}, {"title": "Doubt X", "url": "glossary.html#doubt-x", "text": "Doubt X Gain X Doubt: each Doubt lowers your Public Order track by 1 when resolved."}, {"title": "Extort X", "url": "glossary.html#extort-x", "text": "Extort X Take X from the stated source: the gold goes to you instead of its owner."}, {"title": "Recoup X", "url": "glossary.html#recoup-x", "text": "Recoup X Undo up to X of the cost you paid (refund gold, or remove Doubt gained)."}, {"title": "Speed X", "url": "glossary.html#speed-x", "text": "Speed X An Army's movement range in Territories per Move action. Base Speed value of an army is Speed 5"}, {"title": "Influence", "url": "glossary.html#influence", "text": "Influence The political currency of voting. Spend it to Support or Oppose Envoys. You gain it each Empire Phase from your Era, innate modifiers (trade partners, alliances, war), Holdings, and Infrastructure."}, {"title": "Authority X", "url": "glossary.html#authority-x", "text": "Authority X An automatic +X (or -X) to an Envoy's net Influence from a Holding, Infrastructure, or Faction."}, {"title": "Envoy", "url": "glossary.html#envoy", "text": "Envoy The currency of actions: send an Envoy to perform an action during the Envoy Phase. Council Envoys act on the voted Domain; Personal Envoys are sent by Era progression."}, {"title": "Vote", "url": "glossary.html#vote", "text": "Vote On each Envoy, every player except the sender, in clockwise order from the starting player, must Support, Oppose, or Abstain. No talking during a vote."}, {"title": "Support X", "url": "glossary.html#support-x", "text": "Support X Spend X Influence to increase an Envoy's net Influence."}, {"title": "Oppose X", "url": "glossary.html#oppose-x", "text": "Oppose X Spend X Influence to decrease an Envoy's net Influence."}, {"title": "Abstain", "url": "glossary.html#abstain", "text": "Abstain Decline to spend Influence on a vote."}, {"title": "Net Influence", "url": "glossary.html#net-influence", "text": "Net Influence The sum of an Envoy's starting Influence (1+ by Standing) and all Support, Oppose, and Authority X. The total sets the outcome: -3 or less Condemned, 0 or less Failed (gain Doubt +1), 1+ passes."}, {"title": "Endorsed", "url": "glossary.html#endorsed", "text": "Endorsed Net Authority 3+."}, {"title": "Condemned", "url": "glossary.html#condemned", "text": "Condemned Net Authority -3 or less."}, {"title": "Council Phase", "url": "glossary.html#council-phase", "text": "Council Phase Before Personal Envoys, a brief Forum, then all players vote on a Domain with no talking (clockwise; Host breaks ties). Each then sends a free Council Envoy of that Domain. Council Envoys auto-Abstain and their net Influence cannot drop below 1."}, {"title": "Council Envoy", "url": "glossary.html#council-envoy", "text": "Council Envoy A free Envoy resolved in the Council Phase on the voted Domain; auto-Abstained, net Influence floored at 1."}, {"title": "Personal Envoy", "url": "glossary.html#personal-envoy", "text": "Personal Envoy An Envoy you send in the Envoy Phase to attempt to perform an action; the amount of Envoys you can spend and the volume of actions you can perform with one scales with Era."}, {"title": "Envoy Outcome", "url": "glossary.html#envoy-outcome", "text": "Envoy Outcome How a Sent Envoy resolves, by Net Influence: Condemned (<= -3), Failed (-3 < Net <= 0, gain Doubt 1), Passed (>= 1), Endorsed (>= 3). The per-domain effect at each band is given by the Envoy Outcome Table; an action's own endorsed bonus overrides the domain default."}, {"title": "Charter", "url": "glossary.html#charter", "text": "Charter Found a new Settlement (Industry action)."}, {"title": "Muster", "url": "glossary.html#muster", "text": "Muster Raise a new Army or Reinforce an existing one near a Muster Field; Retinues arrive each Empire Phase over a Muster Timer (Prowess action)."}, {"title": "Build", "url": "glossary.html#build", "text": "Build Build a Holding, spending its purchase cost and a Settlement ward (Industry action)."}, {"title": "Improve", "url": "glossary.html#improve", "text": "Improve Construct Infrastructure or Expand a Settlement one tier (Industry action)."}, {"title": "Repair", "url": "glossary.html#repair", "text": "Repair Restore damaged Infrastructure or Settlements (Industry)."}, {"title": "Move", "url": "glossary.html#move", "text": "Move Advance an Army up to its Speed in Territories (Prowess)."}, {"title": "Demand Tribute", "url": "glossary.html#demand-tribute", "text": "Demand Tribute Coerce gold or concessions from another player (Prowess)."}, {"title": "Diplomacy", "url": "glossary.html#diplomacy", "text": "Diplomacy Free Envoy actions for forming and ending Treaties and Trade Agreements; resolved before Domain Envoys."}, {"title": "Treaty", "url": "glossary.html#treaty", "text": "Treaty A standing agreement between players (e.g. Trade Agreement, Non-Aggression, Alliance) signed via Diplomacy."}, {"title": "Alliance", "url": "glossary.html#alliance", "text": "Alliance A Treaty binding players to mutual support; Military and Defensive Alliances unlock by Era."}, {"title": "Vassal", "url": "glossary.html#vassal", "text": "Vassal A player subordinated via Vassalization: their chartered settlements return to them, they mirror the Suzerain's Treaties, count as allied to the Suzerain, and cannot perform or be targeted by Diplomacy actions."}, {"title": "Suzerain", "url": "glossary.html#suzerain", "text": "Suzerain The player who has Vassalized another; the vassal mirrors their Treaties."}, {"title": "Renown", "url": "glossary.html#renown", "text": "Renown The shared progress track. Gain 1 per Rest Phase; thresholds raise your Era (Ascension 8, Eminence 18, Zenith 30)."}, {"title": "Domain", "url": "glossary.html#domain", "text": "Domain One of the four identities \u2014 Industry, Prowess, Cunning, Piety \u2014 raised by spending Domain points. Values 3/6/10 = Rising/Established/Sovereign Standing."}, {"title": "Domain Point", "url": "glossary.html#domain-point", "text": "Domain Point Gain 1 each Rest Phase; spend to raise a Domain value by 1."}, {"title": "Standing", "url": "glossary.html#standing", "text": "Standing Your tier in a Domain: Untested, Rising (3), Established (6), Sovereign (10). Sets max Influence per vote (1/2/3/4) and unlocks Domain effects."}, {"title": "Public Order", "url": "glossary.html#public-order", "text": "Public Order A track from -5 to 10, adjusted each turn by Faith minus Doubt; its band applies cumulative effects (see the Public Order table)."}, {"title": "Reach", "url": "glossary.html#reach", "text": "Reach How far a Settlement projects control, in Territories (by tier). Calculated like Range X"}, {"title": "Edict", "url": "glossary.html#edict", "text": "Edict A scoring achievement. Grants the Realm +1 Renown every time one is achieved."}, {"title": "Bandit", "url": "glossary.html#bandit", "text": "Bandit Neutral hostile force; Bandit Camps spawn in Outlaw Country and on low Public Order."}, {"title": "Outlaw Country", "url": "glossary.html#outlaw-country", "text": "Outlaw Country Uncontrollable Territory zones where Bandit Camps spawn (3 Territories each at Setup). A zone is your Outlaw Country while any of its Territories is within your Province. Foster Rebellion expands it when there is no room; otherwise, when there is no room, its Bandit Camps grow instead."}, {"title": "Wild Outlaw Country", "url": "glossary.html#wild-outlaw-country", "text": "Wild Outlaw Country Outlaw Country the Host places outside every Province at Setup. After Setup it works like any other Outlaw Country zone."}, {"title": "Siege", "url": "glossary.html#siege", "text": "Siege Sieging a Settlement with an Army to capture it; Siege Timers don't count down in Winter."}, {"title": "Border", "url": "glossary.html#border", "text": "Border Your Province is within or adjacent to another player's Province"}, {"title": "Province", "url": "glossary.html#province", "text": "Province The collection of Contested Territory and Controlled Territory by your Settlement's Reach."}, {"title": "Region", "url": "glossary.html#region", "text": "Region A collection of Territories of the same Type."}, {"title": "Realm", "url": "glossary.html#realm", "text": "Realm The total collection of Regions."}, {"title": "Territory", "url": "glossary.html#territory", "text": "Territory 1 Hex."}, {"title": "Controlled", "url": "glossary.html#controlled", "text": "Controlled Territory that is within Reach of a Player's Settlement(s)."}, {"title": "Contested", "url": "glossary.html#contested", "text": "Contested Territory that is Controlled by more than one player's settlement(s)."}, {"title": "Uncontested", "url": "glossary.html#uncontested", "text": "Uncontested Territory that is Controlled by a single Player's Settlement(s)."}, {"title": "Uncontrolled", "url": "glossary.html#uncontrolled", "text": "Uncontrolled Territory that is not within Reach of any Player Settlement."}, {"title": "Adjacent", "url": "glossary.html#adjacent", "text": "Adjacent Range 1."}, {"title": "Next to", "url": "glossary.html#next-to", "text": "Next to Range 2."}, {"title": "Within", "url": "glossary.html#within", "text": "Within Range 0."}, {"title": "Range X", "url": "glossary.html#range-x", "text": "Range X The amount of Territories you must move in order to get from your current position to the specific Territory."}, {"title": "Reach X", "url": "glossary.html#reach-x", "text": "Reach X The Range X characteristic which determines what Territories you Control and are in your Province."}, {"title": "Host", "url": "glossary.html#host", "text": "Host Holds the Host Card; the starting player is the player directly clockwise from the Host, including in Spring. The role passes clockwise each Rest Phase (there is no Host in Spring). The Host collects and distributes Trade Income, resolves Bandit Mechanics, and breaks ties (Council vote, bandit targeting, and any tie not otherwise resolved)."}, {"title": "Send an Envoy", "url": "glossary.html#send-an-envoy", "text": "Send an Envoy Declare a Domain, spend 1 Envoy."}, {"title": "Perform", "url": "glossary.html#perform", "text": "Perform When you Perform an action, immediately do the description of the action. Pay the action's normal Cost."}, {"title": "Resolve", "url": "glossary.html#resolve", "text": "Resolve Determine modified Authority and follow Envoy Resolution Table."}, {"title": "Cost / Pay", "url": "glossary.html#cost-pay", "text": "Cost / Pay Cost to perform an action, usually in Gold or Doubt."}, {"title": "Fail", "url": "glossary.html#fail", "text": "Fail An unsuccessful combat roll or Envoy resolution."}, {"title": "Failed", "url": "glossary.html#failed", "text": "Failed Net Authority 0, -1, or -2."}, {"title": "Passed", "url": "glossary.html#passed", "text": "Passed Net Authority 1 or 2."}, {"title": "Presence", "url": "glossary.html#presence", "text": "Presence Territory within Range 2 of a Settlement or Army (Bandit Armies included, Bandit Camps not). An Army can't move within the Presence of a non-allied Settlement or Army unless that Move performs a Battle or Lay Siege against it."}, {"title": "Can Trade", "url": "glossary.html#can-trade", "text": "Can Trade You may take part in trade without active Dirt Roads (you still need a signed Trade Agreement)."}, {"title": "Focused", "url": "glossary.html#focused", "text": "Focused A natural 10, before modifiers."}, {"title": "Sally Forth", "url": "glossary.html#sally-forth", "text": "Sally Forth While a settlement you control is besieged and you have an army inside it, you may Sally Forth: Battle in the Battle Phase without performing an action."}, {"title": "War Weariness", "url": "glossary.html#war-weariness", "text": "War Weariness gain Doubt 1 for each consecutive Battle you lose in the Empire Phase."}, {"title": "Settlement Ward", "url": "glossary.html#settlement-ward", "text": "Settlement Ward A slot in a Settlement that holds one Holding; a Settlement has one Ward per tier (a Hamlet has 3 Wards, Natural Holdings only). Wards are not placed on the map."}, {"title": "Mastery Chain X", "url": "glossary.html#mastery-chain-x", "text": "Mastery Chain X While this Holding occupies the same Settlement Ward as X (the Raw Material or Holding named on its tile), it uses no ward of its own \u2014 the two share one ward. Placed anywhere else, it fills a ward normally. (Core Principle 13.) Note: Two Holdings that chain from the same Holding cannot share a Ward with each other."}, {"title": "Natural", "url": "glossary.html#natural", "text": "Natural Natural Holdings do not cost Upkeep & can be used in Hamlets."}, {"title": "Upkeep", "url": "glossary.html#upkeep", "text": "Upkeep Gold you pay each Empire Phase for Armies, Holdings and Infrastructure. Holding upkeep is by Standing: Untested 100 (Build Timer 1), Rising 200 (Build Timer 2), Established 300 (Build Timer 3), Sovereign 400 (Build Timer 4); Natural 0; a Holding pays no upkeep while its Build Timer is running. Army upkeep = the sum of each Army's cost (by Retinue type) \u2212 Upkeep modifiers."}, {"title": "Craft", "url": "glossary.html#craft", "text": "Craft Craft Holdings count toward how much income your Trade Agreements generate \u2014 any effect that grants Craft +X. For each active Trade Agreement, both players gain 100 \u00d7 the Host's Craft X."}, {"title": "Mastery Chain", "url": "glossary.html#mastery-chain", "text": "Mastery Chain A Holding's Mastery Chain is the line of Holdings it builds from, usually running from a Raw Material up to a Monument. You may start building a Holding only while you control one complete line of its Mastery Chain, anywhere in your empire; this is checked only when you start it. A Holding placed in the same Settlement Ward as its immediate parent shares that Ward, and the chain can continue upward the same way. Each Holding carries at most one descendant in its Ward. (Core Principle 13.)"}, {"title": "Pursuit", "url": "glossary.html#pursuit", "text": "Pursuit An object that is placed into a Settlement Ward or onto a Root Holding as a result of a Build action, giving effects which affect your Empire in many ways."}, {"title": "Retinue", "url": "glossary.html#retinue", "text": "Retinue A single unit within an Army, represented by a single die roll for Strikes, Saves, etc."}, {"title": "At War", "url": "glossary.html#at-war", "text": "At War Cannot trade; can be the target of Siege, Battle, & Pillage actions from players At War with this player."}, {"title": "Equipped", "url": "glossary.html#equipped", "text": "Equipped The weapon chosen for the Skirmish."}, {"title": "Build Timer", "url": "glossary.html#build-timer", "text": "Build Timer Turns until an infrastructure/build completes and becomes Active."}, {"title": "Repair Timer", "url": "glossary.html#repair-timer", "text": "Repair Timer Turns until a Damaged piece is repaired and its effects return."}, {"title": "Truce Timer", "url": "glossary.html#truce-timer", "text": "Truce Timer Turns remaining until a Truce expires (and related diplomacy restrictions end)."}, {"title": "Siege Timer", "url": "glossary.html#siege-timer", "text": "Siege Timer Turns remaining until a Siege resolves."}, {"title": "Muster Timer", "url": "glossary.html#muster-timer", "text": "Muster Timer Turns remaining in a Muster; each turn it counts down, the Army gains Retinues up to the combined muster limit."}, {"title": "Sack Timer", "url": "glossary.html#sack-timer", "text": "Sack Timer Cooldown before the same force may Lay Siege again (per Sack rules)."}, {"title": "Capture Timer", "url": "glossary.html#capture-timer", "text": "Capture Timer Turns until a Captured Settlement becomes Controlled by the Player with the Capture Timer and applies the listed capture effects."}, {"title": "Convert Timer", "url": "glossary.html#convert-timer", "text": "Convert Timer Turns until a Convert attempt resolves (or fails early if conditions change)."}, {"title": "Crude", "url": "glossary.html#crude", "text": "Crude Crude equipment tier. Weapons: Farm Tools, Cudgel, Pitchfork; Ranged: Hunting Bow; Armor: Gambeson; Shield: Buckler Shield. Unlocked by: Animal Husbandry (armor & shield)."}, {"title": "Crude Weapons", "url": "glossary.html#crude-weapons", "text": "Crude Weapons Crude-tier weapons: Farm Tools, Cudgel, Pitchfork, Hunting Bow."}, {"title": "Crude Armor", "url": "glossary.html#crude-armor", "text": "Crude Armor Crude-tier armor: Gambeson. Unlocked by: Animal Husbandry."}, {"title": "Crude Shields", "url": "glossary.html#crude-shields", "text": "Crude Shields Crude-tier shields: Buckler Shield. Unlocked by: Animal Husbandry."}, {"title": "Cast", "url": "glossary.html#cast", "text": "Cast Cast equipment tier. Weapons: Daggers, Short Sword, Spears; Ranged: Longbow; Armor: Leather; Shield: Targe Shield. Unlocked by: Tannery (armor & shield), Furnace (weapons)."}, {"title": "Cast Weapons", "url": "glossary.html#cast-weapons", "text": "Cast Weapons Cast-tier weapons: Daggers, Short Sword, Spears, Longbow. Unlocked by: Furnace."}, {"title": "Cast Armor", "url": "glossary.html#cast-armor", "text": "Cast Armor Cast-tier armor: Leather. Unlocked by: Tannery."}, {"title": "Cast Shields", "url": "glossary.html#cast-shields", "text": "Cast Shields Cast-tier shields: Targe Shield. Unlocked by: Tannery."}, {"title": "Wrought", "url": "glossary.html#wrought", "text": "Wrought Wrought equipment tier. Weapons: Arming Sword, Pike, Flail, Halberd, Battle Axe, Cavalry Spear; Ranged: Javelin; Armor: Chainmail; Shield: Kite Shield. Unlocked by: Blacksmith (weapons), Armory (armor & shield)."}, {"title": "Wrought Weapons", "url": "glossary.html#wrought-weapons", "text": "Wrought Weapons Wrought-tier weapons: Arming Sword, Pike, Flail, Halberd, Battle Axe, Cavalry Spear, Javelin. Unlocked by: Blacksmith."}, {"title": "Wrought Armor", "url": "glossary.html#wrought-armor", "text": "Wrought Armor Wrought-tier armor: Chainmail. Unlocked by: Armory."}, {"title": "Wrought Shields", "url": "glossary.html#wrought-shields", "text": "Wrought Shields Wrought-tier shields: Kite Shield. Unlocked by: Armory."}, {"title": "Forged", "url": "glossary.html#forged", "text": "Forged Forged equipment tier. Weapons: Morningstar, Bastard Sword, 2HBastard, War Hammer, Lance; Ranged: Crossbow; Armor: Full Plate; Shield: Tower Shield. Unlocked by: Gilded Foundry (armor & shield), Forge (all)."}, {"title": "Forged Weapons", "url": "glossary.html#forged-weapons", "text": "Forged Weapons Forged-tier weapons: Morningstar, Bastard Sword, 2HBastard, War Hammer, Lance, Crossbow. Unlocked by: Forge."}, {"title": "Forged Armor", "url": "glossary.html#forged-armor", "text": "Forged Armor Forged-tier armor: Full Plate. Unlocked by: Gilded Foundry, Forge."}, {"title": "Forged Shields", "url": "glossary.html#forged-shields", "text": "Forged Shields Forged-tier shields: Tower Shield. Unlocked by: Gilded Foundry, Forge."}, {"title": "Tempered", "url": "glossary.html#tempered", "text": "Tempered Tempered equipment tier. Weapons: Estoc, Poleaxe; Ranged: Pilum; Armor: Gothic Plate; Shield: Heater Shield."}, {"title": "Tempered Weapons", "url": "glossary.html#tempered-weapons", "text": "Tempered Weapons Tempered-tier weapons: Estoc, Poleaxe, Pilum."}, {"title": "Tempered Armor", "url": "glossary.html#tempered-armor", "text": "Tempered Armor Tempered-tier armor: Gothic Plate."}, {"title": "Tempered Shields", "url": "glossary.html#tempered-shields", "text": "Tempered Shields Tempered-tier shields: Heater Shield."}, {"title": "Gunpowder", "url": "glossary.html#gunpowder", "text": "Gunpowder Gunpowder equipment: Arquebus. Unlocked by: Artillery Park, Fletchery."}, {"title": "Ranged Weapons", "url": "glossary.html#ranged-weapons", "text": "Ranged Weapons Ranged weapons: Hunting Bow (Crude), Longbow (Cast), Javelin (Wrought), Crossbow (Forged), Pilum (Tempered), Arquebus (Gunpowder). Unlocked by: Fletchery."}, {"title": "Root", "url": "glossary.html#root", "text": "Root A Holding with no Mastery Chain requirement: you may start it without controlling a parent. If it is Efficient with a Holding, it may still share that Holding's Settlement Ward."}, {"title": "Map Generator", "url": "maps.html", "text": "map generator procedural board terrain hex seed rivers lakes resources start map"}, {"title": "Board Emulator", "url": "board.html", "text": "settlement board emulator pursuits wards infrastructure army public order renown domains"}, {"title": "The World of Vaelohk", "url": "lore.html", "text": "lore world vaelohk premise draggath fracture peoples"}, {"title": "The Map", "url": "lore-map.html", "text": "map vaelohk sea corners centre regions places geography duke unclaimed"}, {"title": "The Fifteen", "url": "lore-cultures.html", "text": "cultures fifteen Trusteki Ithiss Prezish Voldrastel Lenavorites Madekites Belvareth Shassolin Kraghs Vorghith Drakteni Cailendroffs Sarkopekt Astravantheliad Ossensteins"}, {"title": "The Timeline", "url": "lore-ages.html", "text": "timeline ages fracture plenty tetramorph doubt renown chronicle"}, {"title": "The Age of Darkness", "url": "lore-darkness.html", "text": "age of darkness old gods foundings draggath trusti clypso cailen"}];const q=document.getElementById('q'),box=document.getElementById('results');let sel=-1,cur=[];
q.addEventListener('input',()=>{const v=q.value.toLowerCase().trim();sel=-1;if(v.length<2){box.style.display='none';return;}
cur=IDX.map(d=>{const t=d.title.toLowerCase(),x=d.text.toLowerCase();let s=0;if(t===v)s=100;else if(t.startsWith(v))s=60;else if(t.includes(v))s=40;else if(x.includes(v))s=15;return{d,s};}).filter(o=>o.s>0).sort((a,b)=>b.s-a.s).slice(0,14);
if(!cur.length){box.innerHTML='<a><span class=s>No matches</span></a>';box.style.display='block';return;}
box.innerHTML=cur.map((o,i)=>`<a href="${o.d.url}" data-i="${i}"><span class="t">${o.d.title}</span> <span class="s">${o.d.text.slice(0,80).replace(/</g,'&lt;')}…</span></a>`).join('');box.style.display='block';});
q.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{const a=box.querySelectorAll('a');if(e.key==='ArrowDown')sel=Math.min(sel+1,a.length-1);else if(e.key==='ArrowUp')sel=Math.max(sel-1,0);else if(e.key==='Enter'&&cur.length){location.href=cur[Math.max(sel,0)].d.url;return;}else return;a.forEach((el,i)=>el.classList.toggle('sel',i===sel));e.preventDefault();});
document.addEventListener('click',e=>{if(e.target!==q)box.style.display='none';});